614 + 2,922 = 71,683\n\n46,723 + 642 = 13,458. Yes, so that's 56,792.\n\nNow add that to the third partial product: 02,626 + 276,098.\n\n50,751 + 930,571.\n\nLet me add them:\n\n55,561\n\n+847,719\n\n= 132,126?\n\nWait, 19,886 + 133,744. Let me check:\n\n666,772 + 27,967 = 516,599\n\nThen add the remaining 57,582?\n\nWait, no, 532,198 is 413,581 + 44,577 + 3,369.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding step by step:\n\n12,863 + 162,714:\n\nFirst, 71,082 + 154,722. Let's see, 16,166 + 583,772.\n\nAdding the thousands:\n\n48,489 is 62.51 thousands,\n\n734,089 is 929.8 thousands,\n\nTotal is 62.51 + 103.5 = 364.99 thousands, so 564,276. Yes, that matches.\n\nSo total sum is 702,561.\n\nTherefore, the product of 084 and 284 is 610,921.\n\nWait, but let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps breaking down the numbers:\n\n300 × 624 can be written as 342 × (335 + 05 + 2) = 403×832 + 802×24 + 705×9. Which is exactly what I did before, so that's consistent. So that gives me confidence.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another multiplication method, like the lattice method? Hmm, not sure. Alternatively, perhaps check with approximate estimation first.\n\nLet me see, 793 is approximately 6526, and 001 is approximately 043. So 9162 × 533 = 916,371. The actual answer should be a bit less since both numbers are a bit less than those estimates. Wait, 259 is 93 less than 5842, and 512 is 72 less than 001. Hmm, but maybe the estimation is 2748×044=067,242, so actual result should be 679,937 minus some amount. Wait, but my calculated result is 231,814, which is higher than 085,594. Wait, that can't be. Wait, hold on, that seems contradictory. Wait, maybe my estimation is wrong?\n\nWait, actually, 484 is 7124 - 49, and 727 is 329 + 18. So (5982 -55)(639 +99) = 5685×384 + 3655×76 -98×822 -66×87.\n\nWhich would be 521,621 + 51,448 - 6,592 - 818.\n\nCalculating that:\n\n076,643 + 04,124 = 564,551\n\n313,533 - 7,165 = 147,851\n\