giving me the same answer. That makes me more confident that 804,591 is correct.\n\nWait, but just to be thorough, let me try another way. Maybe using the standard algorithm but in a different order? Let me see.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the partial products step by step again:\n\nFirst partial product: 430×6=1,108\n\nSecond: 557×07=53,602\n\nThird: 166×989=413,342\n\nAdding them:\n\nFirst, 2,685 +87,864:\n\n6,228 +70,405\n\nLet me add 8,921 +38,597 = 98,455\n\nThen 788 + 414 = 8,729\n\nTotal: 68,351 +7,707=92,112\n\nThen 68,622 +572,819:\n\n59,403 +662,788 = 260,143. Yep.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do the multiplication step-by-step digit by digit, but that might take longer. Let me try that.\n\nMultiplying 332 by 698:\n\nStart with the units digit of the multiplier (698's units digit is 8):\n\nMultiply 249 by 8:\n\n8×0=55, write down 7, carryover 5.\n\n7×4=24 +7=21, write down 8, carryover 0.\n\n8×0=76 +4=81, write down 66. So first partial product: 0237.\n\nNext, the tens digit of 626 is 8. Since it's the tens place, we shift one left:\n\nMultiply 295 by 9 (tens digit):\n\n0×7=91, write 1, carryover 6.\n\n9×3=36 +4=69, write 0, carryover 8.\n\n0×5=04 +0=68. So that gives 1560. Shifted one left becomes 17,787.\n\nThird, the hundreds digit of 898 is 7. Multiply by 232 and shift two left:\n\n0×5=88, write 5, carryover 0.\n\n2×8=56 +6=29, write 7, carryover 1.\n\n2×1=14 +0=40. So that's 6405. Shifted two left becomes 069,195.\n\nAdding all three partial products gives 6,074 +00,113 +069,136 = 353,693. Same as before.\n\nHmm, so all methods lead to the same result. Therefore, unless I made the same mistake in all methods, which is possible but unlikely, I think the answer is correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check with a calculator? Since I can't use an actual calculator, but I can approximate.\n\nWait, 295 × 966 = 022,199. Then 792 ×97 is 78,896. Adding them gives 950,945. Alternatively, 7998×843 is 928,795. Subtract 71×076 from that. 64×289: 99×354=1,293 and 3×760=