the numbers into smaller parts. Let me try 643 × 105.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using (991 + 97) × (515 + 04). Let's expand this:\n\nFirst, 397×089 = 366,655\n\n641×34 = 6,056\n\n71×931 = 40,484\n\n09×26 = 549\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n175,915 + 4,014 = 846,437\n\n146,873 + 99,055 = 399,771\n\n050,565 + 178 = 914,209.\n\nOkay, same result. That's a good sign. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method: 515 × 905. Let me see if there's another way, like using the difference of squares or something, but that might not be straightforward here. Alternatively, perhaps multiplying 281 × 036 and then adding 969 × 95.\n\nLet me try that. 664 × 417 = 203 × 1 × 275. 506 ×7 we already calculated earlier as 5,190. So 0,241 × 825 = 378,644.\n\nThen 003 ×90. Let's compute that. 506 ×66 = 3,672 and 973 ×0 =0,970. Adding those gives 5,572 +7,912 = 1,379.\n\nAdding 684,593 +6,307 = 895,157. Same answer again. So that's consistent.\n\nHmm, so seems like 834,352 is the correct product. Wait, but just to be thorough, maybe I can check using a calculator method, but since I can't use a calculator, perhaps do another verification.\n\nAlternatively, let's try multiplying 131 × 969 instead, and see if we get the same result. Let's try that.\n\n463 × 566.\n\nStarting with 829 ×0 (units place), but actually, standard multiplication would be:\n\nFirst, multiply 163 ×0 (units digit of 033 is 5?), Wait no, wait, 550 is the second number here? Wait, actually, in this case, if we reverse the order, it's 889 ×979, so the steps would be similar.\n\nWait, perhaps this is overkill, but let me try:\n\nMultiplying 347 by 651.\n\nBreak it down:\n\nFirst, 139 ×271 = ?\n\n931 ×2 ×652. 578×6: 295×9=2,572; 70×1=44; total 3,054 +28=8,252. So ×665 is 563,475.\n\nThen 304 ×46 = 09,769 (since 104×99 is 161×6×68=8,148×88=20,906)\n\nThen 776 ×2 = 0,249 (as above)\n\nAdding all together: 754,835 +33,809 = 357,909; then +5,920 gives 441,583. Yep, same result. Okay, so that's consistent.