      "text": "73320 - 1833 = 71487.\n   \\].\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 611 and 117 is \\(\\boxed{71487}\\).\n\nHowever, upon re-evaluating the problem, it seems there was a miscalculation in the final answer. The correct product of 611 and 117 is actually calculated as follows:\n\nUsing direct multiplication:\n\\[\n611 \\times 117 = 611 \\times (100 + 10 + 7) = 611 \\times 100 + 611 \\times 10 + 611 \\times 7 = 61100 + 6110 + 4277 = 71487\n\\]\n\nThus, the correct final answer is \\(\\boxed{71487}\\).",
