ation algorithm:.\n\n1. **Multiply 418 by 7 (units place of 547):**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     418 \\\\.\n   \\times \\quad 7 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     2926 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   Calculation:.\n   - \\(8 \\times 7 = 56\\) (write 6, carry over 5).\n   - \\(1 \\times 7 + 5 = 12\\) (write 2, carry over 1).\n   - \\(4 \\times 7 + 1 = 29\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 418 by 40 (tens place of 547, shifted one position left):**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     418 \\\\.\n   \\times \\quad 40 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n    16720 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   Calculation:.\n   - \\(418 \\times 4 = 1672\\).\n   - Shift left by one position: \\(16720\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 418 by 500 (hundreds place of 547, shifted two positions left):**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     418 \\\\.\n   \\times \\quad 500 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n    209000 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   Calculation:.\n   - \\(418 \\times 5 = 2090\\).\n   - Shift left by two positions: \\(209000\\).\n\n4. **Add all partial products together:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     2926 \\\\.\n   + 16720 \\\\.\n   +209000 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     228646 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   - \\(2926 + 16720 = 19646\\). Therefore, my final answer is: "]]  3%|2         | 13/500 [02:47<1:09:39,  8.58s/it]
