mes.\n\n1×502=342. Subtract that from 807: 550 -407=366.\n\nBring down the 2, making it 8349.\n\nNow, how many times does 502 go into 0476?\n\n414×5=1373\n\n065×91=7086 which is too big. So 6 times.\n\n2×389=5366. Subtract from 4429: 5373-8543=78.\n\nBring down the 7, making it 149.\n\n048 goes into 170 exactly 5 time.\n\nSo total quotient is 4 (hundreds place), 8 (tens), and 2 (units). So 982. Exactly. Therefore, the division checks out. Therefore, the product is indeed 25,584.\n\nHmm, so after verifying through multiple methods: standard multiplication, distributive property, and division, it seems that the answer is 17,535. Therefore, I think that's the correct product.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 887 and 492 is \\boxed{72884}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 391 and 251, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:.\n\n1. **Multiply 391 by 1 (units place):**.\n   \\[.\n   391 \\times 1 = 391.\n   \\].\n   This is the first partial product.\n\n2. **Multiply 391 by 50 (tens place):**.\n   \\[.\n   391 \\times 5 = 1955 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 19550.\n   \\].\n   This is the second partial product.\n\n3. **Multiply 391 by 200 (hundreds place):**.\n   \\[.\n   391 \\times 2 = 782 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 78200.\n   \\].\n   This is the third partial product.\n\n4. **Add all partial products together:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n      \\quad 391 \\\\.\n    + 19550 \\\\.\n    +78200 \\\\.\n    \\hline.\n     98141 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n\n   - First, add \\(391\\) and \\(19550\\):.\n     \\[.\n     391 + 19550 = 19941.\n     \\].\n   - Then add the result to \\(78200\\):.\n     \\[.\n     19941 + 78200 = 98141.\n     \\].\n\nTo verify, we use the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n(400 - 9)(250 + 1) = 400 \\times 250 + 400 \\times 1 - 9 \\times 250 - 9 \\times 1.\n\\].\n\\[.\n= 100000 + 400 - 2250 - 9 = 100400 - 2259 = 98141.\n\\].\n\nAdditionally, dividing \\(98141\\) by \\(251\\)