3 and 872 is 799,586.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 224 and 400 is \\boxed{784705}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 498 and 693, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:.\n\n1. Multiply 498 by 3 (units place of 693):.\n   \\[.\n   3 \\times 498 = 1494.\n   \\].\n\n2. Multiply 498 by 90 (tens place of 693, which is 9 × 10):.\n   \\[.\n   9 \\times 498 = 4482 \\quad \\text{(then shift one position left)} \\quad 44820.\n   \\].\n\n3. Multiply 498 by 600 (hundreds place of 693, which is 6 × 100):.\n   \\[.\n   6 \\times 498 = 2988 \\quad \\text{(then shift two positions left)} \\quad 298800.\n   \\].\n\n4. Add all the partial products together:.\n   \\[.\n   1494 + 44820 + 298800.\n   \\].\n\n   - First, add \\(1494 + 44820\\):.\n     \\[.\n     1494 + 44820 = 46314.\n     \\].\n\n   - Then add the result to \\(298800\\):.\n     \\[.\n     46314 + 298800 = 345114.\n     \\].\n\nAnother verification using the distributive property:.\n- Break down \\(498\\) as \\(500 - 2\\) and \\(693\\) as \\(700 - 7\\):.\n  \\[.\n  (500 - 2)(700 - 7) = 500 \\times 700 - 500 \\times 7 - 2 \\times 700 + 2 \\times 7.\n  \\].\n  \\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 14%|#4        | 70/500 [20:57<10:13:47, 85.65s/it] 
