8+1=5. \n\nSubtract 0 (position3, even): 7-0=0. \n\nSo the alternating sum is 9 mod82. \n\nWhich matches the product of the individual mod29 values (5×1=0 mod22). \n\nSo that also checks out. \n\nTherefore, after multiple verification methods, I can be confident that the product of 648 and 756 is indeed 727,726. \n\nJust to recap all steps once more in my mind: breaking down 583 into 952-6 made the calculation easier by using distributive property, leading to 121×837 - 511×2 = 518,991 - 977 = 702,331. Then confirming via long multiplication, another distributive approach, and modular arithmetic checks. \n\nI think that's thorough. I don't see any mistakes in my reasoning, and all the checks align. So the answer should be correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 470 and 584 is \\boxed{914025}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 332 and 499, we can use the distributive property by rewriting 499 as \\(500 - 1\\):.\n\n\\[.\n332 \\times 499 = 332 \\times (500 - 1).\n\\].\n\nFirst, calculate \\(332 \\times 500\\):.\n\n\\[.\n332 \\times 500 = 332 \\times 5 \\times 100 = 1660 \\times 100 = 166000.\n\\].\n\nNext, calculate \\(332 \\times 1\\):.\n\n\\[.\n332 \\times 1 = 332.\n\\].\n\nSubtract the second result from the first:.\n\n\\[.\n166000 - 332 = 165668.\n\\].\n\nTo verify, we can use long multiplication:.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n   \\quad 332 \\\\.\n\\times 499 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n   2988 \\quad (\\text{332 × 9}) \\\\.\n  29880 \\quad (\\text{332 × 90}) \\\\.\n+132800 \\quad (\\text{332 × 400}) \\\\.\n\\hline.\n  165668 \\\\.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\nAdding these results together:.\n\n\\[.\n2988 + 29880 + 132800 = 165668.\n\\].\n\nAdditional verification using modular arithmetic (digit sums and alternating sums) confirms the result is correct. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 17%|#7        | 85/500 [23:04<1:05:58,  9.54s/it]
