oduct of 910 and 981, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify the result using multiple methods:.\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n        910 \\\\.\n      \\times 981 \\\\.\n      \\hline.\n        910 \\quad \\text{(910 × 1)} \\\\.\n      + 72800 \\quad \\text{(910 × 80)} \\\\.\n      + 819000 \\quad \\text{(910 × 900)} \\\\.\n      \\hline.\n        892710 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   - Compute each partial product:.\n     - \\(910 \\times 1 = 910\\).\n     - \\(910 \\times 80 = 72800\\).\n     - \\(910 \\times 900 = 819000\\).\n   - Sum the partial products:.\n     - \\(910 + 72800 = 73710\\).\n     - \\(73710 + 819000 = 892710\\).\n\n2. **Distributive Property Expansion:**.\n   \\[.\n   (900 + 10) \\times (900 + 80 + 1) = 900 \\times 900 + 900 \\times 80 + 900 \\times 1 + 10 \\times 900 + 10 \\times 80 + 10 \\times 1.\n   \\].\n   - Compute each term:.\n     - \\(900 \\times 900 = 810000\\).\n     - \\(900 \\times 80 = 72000\\).\n     - \\(900 \\times 1 = 900\\).\n     - \\(10 \\times 900 = 9000\\).\n     - \\(10 \\times 80 = 800\\).\n     - \\(10 \\times 1 = 10\\).\n   - Sum all terms:.\n     - \\(810000 + 72000 = 882000\\).\n     - \\(882000 + 900 = 882900\\).\n     - \\(882900 + 9000 = 891900\\).\n     - \\(891900 + 800 = 892700\\).\n     - \\(892700 + 10 = 892710\\).\n\n3. **Difference of Squares Identity:**.\n   \\[.\n   (a \\times b) = \\left( \\frac{a + b}{2} \\right)^2 - \\left( \\frac{a - b}{2} \\right)^2.\n   \\].\n   - Let \\(a = 910\\) and \\(b = 981\\):.\n     - \\(\\frac{910 + 981}{2} = 945.5\\).\n     - \\(\\frac{910 - 981}{2} = -35.5\\).\n   - Compute squares:.\n     - \\((945.5)^2 = 893970.25\\).\n     - \\((35.5)^2 = 1260.25\\).\n   - Subtract the squares:.\n     - \\(893970.25 - 1260. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 19%|#9        | 96/500 [24:48<31:33,  4.69s/it]
