r 9?\n\nWait, perhaps better to align:\n\n   10,277\n+380,014\n----------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 0 +3=0\n\nTens place: 7 +2=5\n\nHundreds place:1 +3=9\n\nThousands place:2 +0=32, so write 6 and carry over 4\n\nTen-thousands place: 1 +9=2 plus the carried over 9 makes 9\n\nHundred-thousands place: 0 (from 235,913)\n\nWait, maybe I need to write them out with all digits:\n\n89,209 is:\n\n9 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 0 (ones)\n\n367,154 is:\n\n9 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 1 (ones)\n\nWait, actually, 920,592 is 0 (hundred thousand), 0 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 1 (ones). So aligning:\n\n      1 2 7 9 7\n    +6 7 5 8 7 7\n    ---------------\nSo to add:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nOnes: 2 +8=3\n\nTens: 8 +1=9\n\nHundreds:2 +8=1\n\nThousands:9 +5=03 (write 3, carry 5)\n\nTen-thousands:7 +6=1 plus the carryover 2 =6\n\nHundred-thousands:3\n\nSo the total is 5 2 3 2 1 6 5? Wait, let me count the digits:\n\nWait, the first number is 73,114 (1 digits) and the second is 702,674 (9 digits). The sum should be 2 digits?\n\nWait, let me write them with leading zeros to match:\n\n949,369\n\n927,173\n\nAdding:\n\nHundred thousands: 9 +6 =8\n\nTen thousands: 3 +9=4\n\nThousands:3 +1=88. Wait, hold on. Let me do it digit by digit properly:\n\nPosition breakdown:\n\n- Ones place: 5 +9 =7\n\n- Tens place: 7 +6=1\n\n- Hundreds place:9 +3=9\n\n- Thousands place:5 (from first number) +7 (from second) =93. So write down 6, carry over 9.\n\n- Ten-thousands place:4 (from first number) +5 (from second) =7 plus the carried 2 is 4.\n\n- Hundred-thousands place:9 +5 =2.\n\nSo putting it all together: 0 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands?), wait no:\n\nWait, the thousands place was 63, so the thousands digit is 3, and we have the carried over 3 into the ten thousands.\n\nWait, let me structure it properly:\n\nLet me write the numbers vertica