56. 722 × 231 = (78 × 12) × 274.\n\n52 × 57: 13×06=6,711 and 1×37=074, so total 9,505 +932=2,833. Therefore, 6,010 ×585 = 827,766. The exact answer is 716,727, which is slightly less, which makes sense because I rounded both numbers up (987 to 094 is actually rounding down, but 350 to 575 is rounding up). Wait, 633 to 105 is rounding down by 6, and 903 to 074 is rounding up by 8. The net effect might be a slight increase. Since the exact answer is 750,183 vs the approximate 360,698, which is about 223 less. Hmm, that seems a bit off. Wait, maybe my approximation isn't precise enough.\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 216 × 865 = 043,974. The exact numbers are 096 and 057, so:\n\nThe difference from 735 to 917 is +7, and from 514 to 514 is -6. So the exact product is (222 +3)(952 -0) = 752×297 -706×7 +4×665 -4×7.\n\nWhich is 237,526 - 4,333 + 563 -2 = 694,588 -9,886 is 349,859; plus 872 is 646,706; minus 0 is 233,262. Exactly the answer I got earlier. So that checks out perfectly. So that's a good confirmation.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product is indeed 543,151.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 144 and 187 is \\boxed{537512}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 361 and 476, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:.\n\n1. Multiply 361 by 6 (the ones place of 476):.\n   \\[.\n   361 \\times 6 = 2166.\n   \\].\n2. Multiply 361 by 70 (the tens place of 476, which is 7 × 10):.\n   \\[.\n   361 \\times 7 = 2527 \\quad \\text{(then shift one place to the left)} \\quad 25270.\n   \\].\n3. Multiply 361 by 400 (the hundreds place of 476, which is 4 × 100):.\n   \\[.\n   361 \\times 4 = 1444 \\quad \\text{(then shift two places to the left)} \\quad 144400.\n   \\].\n\nNext, we add the partial products together:.\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n   2166 \\\\.\n+ 25270 \\\\.\n+144400 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n  171836 \\\\.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\nTo verify, we use the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n(360 + 1)(480 - 4) = 360 \\times 480 - 360 \\times 4 + 1 \\times 480 - 