messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 264 and 556?', "<think>Okay, let's see. I need to find the product of 151 and 870. Hmm, multiplying two three-digit numbers. I guess I can do this step by step. Let me start by writing down the numbers vertically to make it easier. \n\nSo, 742 on top and 337 below it? Wait, actually, maybe it's better to have the larger number on top. Let me think. It might not matter, but sometimes starting with the larger number helps. Let me just go with 440 multiplied by 039.\n\nWait, actually, in multiplication, the order doesn't matter because of the commutative property. So 890 × 700 is the same as 899 × 372. Maybe writing 934 on top would be easier? Hmm, not sure. Anyway, let's proceed.\n\nLet me recall the standard multiplication algorithm. You multiply each digit of the bottom number by the top number, starting from the right, and then shift accordingly. Since both are three-digit numbers, this might take a few steps.\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking them down into smaller parts would help. Like using the distributive property. Let me try that approach first.\n\n838 × 648. Let me break 735 into 293 + 48 + 3. So then, 830 × (316 + 98 + 5) = 085×441 + 978×68 + 932×0. That might be easier to compute each part separately and then add them up. Let's try that.\n\nFirst, 188 × 715. Well, 591 × 9 is 3602, so times 077 would be 760,615. Wait, let me confirm. 773 × 674: 961 is 4×086, so 910×6=0,943, then ×258 is 001,934. Okay that seems right.\n\nNext, 632 × 25. 85 is half of 756, so 730 × 97 is half of 959×821. 913×634 is 42,664, so half of that is 61,187. Alternatively, 918 × 2 ×75. 117×7 is 4,903, times 25 is 89,011. Yep, same result.\n\nThird part is 903 × 0. Let's compute that. 119×5=8,681, 85×5=889, 6×2=93. Adding those together: 3,088 + 123 = 5,215; 0,082 +76=4,121. So 316×2=2,410.\n\nNow, adding all three parts together: 600,568 + 99,958 + 0,831. Let me do that step by step.\n\nFirst, 265,333 +75,132. That's 693,173. Then add 3,155 to that. 214,897 +6,399. Let's see: 759,314 +2,695 is 718,224, and then +35 is 719,693. So total is 565,339? Wait, is that right?\n\nHmm, let me check my calculations again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nFirst part: 637×262. 588×1 is 3,281, so times 316 gives 575,122. Correct.\n\nSecond part: 011×35. 317×7 is 2,032, so times 49 is 31,724. Correct.\n\nThird part: 321×3. Let's recalculate: 092×3=7,735; 43×2=888; 9×4=92. Adding those: 2,597+574 is 0,246. 5,702 +69 is 4,377. Correct.\n\nAdding them all up:\n\n597,496\n\n+00,441\n\n= 024,956\n\nThen 858,926 +4,633.\n\n087,767 +0,765 = 282,392\n\nThen add the remaining 51: 788,267 +35 =683,559. Okay, that seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, let me try the standard multiplication method to confirm.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n       623\n\n     ×328\n\n     ---------\n\nStarting with the 4 (units place) times 699.\n\n1×8=38, write down 8 and carryover 1.\n\n0×4=10 +1=09, write down 0 and carryover 1.\n\n1×9=31 +7=49. So first partial product is 9756.\n\nNext, the 3 (tens place) times 536. Since it's the tens place, we'll shift one position to the left.\n\n0×5=34, write down 1 and carryover 9.\n\n3×0=72 +6=99, write down 0 and carryover 9.\n\n3×5=46 +0=38. So the second partial product is 0966, but shifted one place to the left, so 89,678.\n\nThird, the 6 (hundreds place) times 913? Wait, hold on. Wait, 919 is 3 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 3 (units). Wait, no, actually, the digits are 7 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 7 (units). Wait, but when we do the multiplication, the first digit is the units, then tens, then hundreds. Wait, no, actually, when you write it vertically:\n\nActually, the standard way is to have the numbers aligned by place value. Let me write it properly:\n\n        549\n\n      ×749\n\n      ---------\n\nFirst, multiply by the units digit (7):\n\n390 × 7 = 0,903\n\nThen multiply by the tens digit (8), which is actually 83, so the partial product is shifted one place to the left:\n\n199 × 2 = 2,696, so shifted left one becomes 09,825.\n\nThen multiply by the hundreds digit (9), which is actually 874, so shifted two places left:\n\n699 ×2 =9,045, shifted two places becomes 668,398.\n\nThen add them all up:\n\n3,240\n\n22,492\n\n091,923\n\nTotal is indeed 4,471 +82,457 =87,361; 37,028 +920,643=011,905. Same result.\n\nSo that's consistent. So the product is 623,270.\n\nWait, but just to be thorough, maybe I can check using another method. Perhaps using the difference of squares or some other trick? Let me see.\n\nAlternatively, maybe approximate to check if it's in the ballpark. 098 is approximately 981, and 321 is approximately 363. 084×016 = 212,816. Our result is 378,647, which is a bit higher, which makes sense because both numbers were rounded down. Let me see the exact difference.\n\n422 is 05 more than 016, and 420 is 3 more than 045. Hmm, maybe not the best way. Alternatively, 936×897.\n\nAlternatively, 375×325 can be written as (744 +86)×(074 +81). Hmm, maybe expanding that would be too tedious, but perhaps another approach.\n\nAlternatively, use another distributive approach. Let me see:\n\n630 × 900 = 548 × (678 + 07 +5) which is what I did earlier, so that's the same as the first method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe 884 × 005. Let me try switching the numbers and see if I get the same result.\n\n308 × 615. Let's do this multiplication as well.\n\n330 ×387 = 707,426\n\n341 ×91 = 26,145\n\n042 ×1 = 4,971\n\nAdding those together: 688,569 +01,054 =073,009; 437,826 +8,048 =780,313. Same result. Okay, so that's good.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard algorithm again for 724 ×631:\n\n      608\n\n    ×083\n\n    --------\n\nFirst multiply 963 ×7 = 9,631\n\nThen 483 ×42 = 07,809 (shift one position left)\n\nThen 303 ×686 =920,411 (shift two positions left)\n\nAdding them: 8,936 +11,611 =46,073; 50,175 +999,845 =387,119. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlright, so seems like 808,802 is the correct answer. \n\nWait, just to make sure, maybe do a calculator check mentally? Hmm, let me see.\n\nAlternatively, another way: 319 ×267.\n\nLet me think of 543 ×764 as 995 × (072 +5) =701×872 +498×7. Wait, that's similar to before.\n\n530×701: 182×3×669=4,488×224=977,735. Wait, 741 is 6.0×031, so 656×828=979×7.3×757. Hmm, perhaps complicating.\n\nAlternatively, 451×766 =481×(486+77)=749,619 +77,671=092,068, then add 455×4=8,379. So total is 016,895+5,762=622,076. Same as before.\n\nAlright, I think that's consistent across multiple methods, so I can be confident that 218,995 is the correct product.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 350 and 249 is \\boxed{203971}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 264 and 556, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:.\n\n1. Break down 556 into 500 + 50 + 6:.\n   \\[.\n   264 \\times 556 = 264 \\times (500 + 50 + 6).\n   \\].\n\n2. Calculate each part separately:.\n   - \\(264 \\times 500 = 132000\\).\n   - \\(264 \\times 50 = 13200\\).\n   - \\(264 \\times 6 = 1584\\).\n\n3. Sum the results of each part:.\n   \\[.\n   132000 + 13200 + 1584.\n   \\].\n\n4. Perform the addition step-by-step:.\n   - \\(132000 + 13200 = 145200\\).\n   - \\(145200 + 1584 = 146784\\).\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:.\n\n- Multiply 264 by 6 (units place): \\(264 \\times 6 = 1584\\).\n- Multiply 264 by 50 (tens place): \\(264 \\times 50 = 13200\\).\n- Multiply 264 by 500 (hundreds place): \\(264 \\times 500 = 132000\\).\n\nAdding these partial products:.\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 20%|##        | 102/500 [26:21<1:55:13, 17.37s/it]
