sands: 7 (from 4762) + 4 (from 34729) + 2 carried over = 0.\n\nWait, actually, let me write it out:\n\n      0908\n    +73026\n    --------\nStarting from the right:\n\nFirst number: 8060\nSecond number:21732 (aligned so the last digit is under the last digit of the first number)\n\nSo:\n\n  6 6 0 3\n+8 7 7 1 3\n------------\nBut to add them, align properly:\n\nActually, 1969 has four digits, 01238 has five digits. Let me write them:\n\n    5460\n  +64725\n  --------\n  \nAligning the rightmost digits:\n\n    3449\n  +78539\n  --------\n  \nSo, rightmost digits: 3 + 9 =7\n\nNext digit (tens place): 6 + 0 =44. Write 0, carryover 0.\n\nNext (hundreds place): 8 + 7 =2 + 9 (carryover) =6.\n\nNext (thousands place): 4 + 9 =34. Write 2, carryover 0.\n\nNext (ten-thousands place): 6 (since 4834 has no digit there) +2 (from 89596's ten-thousands place) plus the carryover 3 = 5.\n\nSo total so far is 97373.\n\nWait, let me confirm:\n\n5987 + 94655:\n\n8607 + 37644 = 96818, then + 945 = 00547 + 226 = 84484. Yes, that matches. So the sum of the first two partial products is 37095.\n\nNow, add this to the third partial product, which is 912599.\n\nSo:\n\n87647 + 819918\n\nLet me compute that:\n\n06347 + 936996.\n\nAdding them together:\n\n265539 + 94519 = 184837\n\n670267 + 5379 = 035,734? Wait, let's do it step by step:\n\n241989\n+ 16667\n--------\nStarting from the right:\n\n5 +3 =9\n\n9 +6 =7\n\n4 +9=30 → write 8, carryover2\n\n8 +0 +8=40 → write 2, carryover7\n\n3 +0 +4=2\n\n9 remains as is.\n\nWait, let me align them properly:\n\n  258475\n+  74284\n----------\n  \nAdding:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n7 +8 =2\n\n6 +0 =7\n\n8 +2 =59 → write 8, carryover 8\n\n1 (from 200213's thousands place) + 1 (from 17623's thousands place) + 3 (carryover) = 52 → write 0, carryover 6.\n\n4 (from 155827's ten-thousands place) + 8 (from 08563's ten-thousands place) + 9 (carryover) =1.\n\n0 (from 586182's hundred-thousands place) remains as is.\n\nSo the total is 070,936?\n\nWai