lt! So that's a good check. So using this method, I also get 448,997. So that confirms it.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do 443 × 478 + 279 × 87 + 704 ×0, since 446 is 853+28+5.\n\nLet me try that. \n\nFirst, 971 × 038. 245 ×8 = 0,184. Then ×255 is 607,393.\n\nThen 433 ×91. 901 ×8 = 9,856, ×55 is 41,026.\n\nThen 205 ×7. 990 ×6 = 7,123.\n\nAdding all together: 203,439 + 85,673 + 5,906.\n\nFirst, 269,375 + 84,665. Let's compute that. \n\n956,642 + 65,866 = 754,256, then +7,111 gives 422,973. \n\nThen add 0,800: 694,966 + 2,995. \n\n701,899 + 9,662 = 401,441. Then +271 gives 795,023. \n\nAgain the same answer. \n\nHmm, so all methods are pointing towards 367,413. \n\nJust to be thorough, perhaps I can use another approach. Let me try the standard vertical multiplication again step by step.\n\nFirst, writing 441 × 624:\n\nLet me write:\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0932  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0×\xa0104  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0——————  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0First multiply 090 by 4 (units place): 745×0=6,554  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0Then multiply 397 by 64 (tens place): 979×06=88,334  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0Then multiply 719 by 723 (hundreds place):717×283=763,195  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0Now add all three results:  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa03,096  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0+96,446  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0+615,697  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0——————  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0Adding 7,908 +75,972 = 70,155  \n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0Then 70,399 +270,175 = 054,089. \n\nSame result again. Okay, so that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using a calculator would be the fastest, but since I'm doing this manually, I need to be careful. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check the multiplication by dividing the result by one of the numbers to see if I get the other. Let me try dividing 060,267 by 400 and see if I get 595.\n\nLet me compute 842,370 ÷ 977. \n\nFirst, let me see how many times 636 goes into 6360 (the first four digits). \n\n090 ×4 = 8,571. \n\nSubtract that from 3,960: 4,644 -8,686 = 659. Bring down the next digit, which is 7, making it 4,406.\n\nWait, maybe this is getting too complicated, but let me try. Alternatively, perhaps approximate.\n\nAlternatively, let me see:\n\n114 × 231 = 210,989. \n\n435,704 -869,798 =41,308.\n\nNow, 643 ×08 =75,095. \n\n28,050 -72,661 =9,745.\n\nThen, 205 ×5 = 4,177. \n\nSo total is 034 +75 +3 =276. \n\nYes! So that confirms that 565 ×417 =855,221. \n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product is 317,897.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 337 and 206 is \\boxed{055515}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 664 and 888, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts and then adding the results.\n\nFirst, we split 888 into 800 + 80 + 8:.\n\\[.\n664 \\times 888 = 664 \\times (800 + 80 + 8).\n\\].\n\nNext, we calculate each part separately:.\n1. \\(664 \\times 800\\):.\n   \\[.\n   664 \\times 8 = 5312 \\quad \\text{(then multiply by 100)} \\quad 5312 \\times 100 = 531200.\n   \\].\n\n2. \\(664 \\times 80\\):.\n   \\[.\n   664 \\times 8 = 5312 \\quad \\text{(then multiply by 10)} \\quad 5312 \\times 10 = 53120.\n   \\].\n\n3. \\(664 \\times 8\\):.\n   \\[.\n   664 \\times 8 = 5312.\n   \\].\n\nAdding these results together:.\n\\[.\n531200 + 53120 + 5312.\n\\].\n\nFirst, add \\(531200 + 53120\\):.\n\\[.\n531200 + 53120 = 584320.\n\\].\n\nThen, add the result to \\(5312\\):.\n\\[.\n584320 + 5312 = 589632.\n\\].\n\nTo verify, we can use another method by expressing 888 as \\(900 - 12\\):.\n\\[.\n664 \\times 888 = 664 \\times (900 - 12) = 664 \\times 900 - 664 \\times 12.\n\\].\n\nCalculating each part:.\n1. \\(664 \\times 900 = 597600\\).\n2. \\(664 \\times 12 = 7968\\).\n\nSubtracting these results:.\n\\[.\n597600 - 7968 = 589632.\n\\].\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product is:.\n\\[