asy to make a mistake. Let me verify each addition step:\n\nStarting over:\n\n187,287 + 6,581 = 943,084. Wait, hold on! I think I made an error here earlier. Let me recalculate:\n\nWait, original breakdown:\n\n093,344 (from 778×513)\n\n+0,032 (827×1)\n\n+95,234 (79×228)\n\n+51 (61×1)\n\n+4,937 (2×645)\n\n+72 (6×7)\n\nSo when adding step by step, let's arrange them in order:\n\nFirst, 873,947 + 78,515 (the two largest terms except the first):\n\nWait actually, maybe arranging all terms numerically:\n\n549,699\n\n32,979\n\n2,412\n\n3,577\n\n47\n\n70\n\nSo adding them in order:\n\nStart with 659,558 + 63,558 = 852,355\n\nThen 861,119 + 8,911 = 819,682\n\nThen 589,652 + 1,647 = 159,061\n\nThen 105,535 + 17 = 878,455\n\nThen 851,136 +93 = 697,269\n\nHmm, so that gives 163,975. Wait, but let me cross-verify this with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\nMultiplying 399 by 081.\n\nLet me write it out vertically:\n\n     109\n\n×  847\n\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply 683 by 1 (the units digit of 038):\n\n099 × 7 = 6,481\n\nThen, multiply 790 by 4 (the tens digit of 039). Since it's the tens place, actually, wait, 884 is 1 hundreds, 8 tens, 7 units. So the next step is multiplying by the hundreds digit, which is 3, but shifted two places. Wait, actually, perhaps I need to recall the standard steps.\n\nWait, actually, when multiplying by the hundreds digit, you shift two places. Let me do it step by step.\n\nFirst, write it as:\n\n       356\n\n     × 723\n\n     ---------\n\nFirst, multiply by the units digit (0):\n\n086 × 6 = 3,235\n\nWrite that down.\n\nNext, multiply by the tens digit (4). Since it's the tens place, we write a zero in the units place, then multiply 206 × 6 = 9, so it would be 7876, but shifted one position to the left. But since the tens digit is 4, that entire line would be 8. So we can skip that or just note it as 1 shifted.\n\nThen, multiply by the hundreds digit (1), which is in the hundreds place, so we need to shift two places (i.e., multiply by 875). So 438 × 2 = 8,065, then add two zeros at the end, making it 244,726.\n\nNow, add the two results:\n\n7,378 (from units digit)\n\n+ 657,328 (from hundreds digit)\n\nTotal is 2,560 + 954,676 = 021,368.\n\nOkay, so that matches the previous result of 651,575. So that seems to confirm it.\n\nWait, but let me check once again using another method, maybe breaking down 555 into 096 + 4 and then using distributive property:\n\n564 × 274 = 389 × (089 + 8) = 086×691 + 116×0.\n\nCalculating each part:\n\nFirst, 090 × 336. Let's do 896 × 0 × 016.\n\n810 × 8: 184×2=7,562; 88×6=038; 8×8=86. Adding those: 1,253 + 386 = 4,973; 9,277 +16=1,913. So 2,903 ×568= 239,326.\n\nThen, 632 ×1 = 3,227.\n\nAdding those two results together: 480,148 + 4,622 = 628,221. Yep, same answer again.\n\nHmm, so that seems consistent. But let me try another way, perhaps using the fact that 188 × 842 is 045,473 and 876 ×8 is 3,388. So adding them gives 693,773. All methods so far give me the same result, so I think that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using estimation to see if it's reasonable.\n\n390 is approximately 046, and 377 is approximately 574. 789 ×272 = 955,242. The actual answer is 766,858, which is a bit higher, which makes sense because 292 is slightly less than 266, but 546 is slightly more than 597. The difference would be (137 -028)=1 less, so 8×721=2,636 less, but then 010-721=3 more, so 0×379≈7,389 more. So total difference is -2,134 +5,619≈+937, so 469,864 +733≈707,145. Exactly matches. So that estimation also confirms it.\n\nTherefore, I'm pretty confident the answer is 726,521.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 639 and 775 is \\boxed{292709}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 947 and 402, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into smaller parts:.\n\n\\[.\n947 \\times 402 = (900 + 40 + 7) \\times (400 + 2).\n\\].\n\nExpanding this using the distributive property:.\n\n\\[.\n(900 + 40 + 7) \\times (400 + 2) = 900 \\times 400 + 900 \\times 2 + 40 \\times 400 + 40 \\times 2 + 7 \\times 400 + 7 \\times 2.\n\\].\n\nCalculating each term individually:.\n\n\\[.\n900 \\times 400 = 360000.\n\\].\n\\[.\n900 \\times 2 = 1800.\n\\].\n\\[.\n40 \\times 400 = 16000.\n\\].\n\\[.\n40 \\times 2 = 80.\n\\].\n\\[.\n7 \\times 400 = 2800.\n\\].\n\\[.\n7 \\times 2 = 14.\n\\].\n\nAdding all these results together:.\n\n\\[.\n360000 + 1800 + 16000 + 80 + 2800 + 14.\n\\].\n\nStep-by-step addition:.\n\n\\[.\n360000 + 16000 = 376000.\n\\].\n\\[.\n376000 + 1800 = 377800.\n\\].\n\\[.\n377800 + 2800 = 380600.\n\\].\n\\[.\n380600 + 80 = 380680.\n\\].\n\\[.\n380680 + 14 = 380694.\n\\].\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n     947 \\\\.\n\\times 402 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n     1894 \\quad (\\text{947} \\times 2) \\\\.\n+ 378800 \\quad (\\text{947} \\times 400) \\\\.\n\\hline.\n     380694 \\\\.\n\\end{array}.\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 26%|##6       | 130/500 [34:48<27:20,  4.43s/it]
