at seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do it another way: 036 × 995 = ?\n\nLet me try using another method, like the distributive property: (256 +17 +7)(287 +51 +7). Expanding this would give all combinations:\n\n246×916 + 182×94 + 889×9 + 48×547 + 79×57 +42×1 +7×757 +8×24 +5×3.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n374×054 = 068,362  \n177×78 = 71,439  \n039×9 = 1,838  \n81×696 =50,386  \n73×12 =2,317  \n46×1 =287  \n6×553 =311  \n1×97 =25  \n4×1 =42  \n\nNow add all these up:\n\nStart with the largest terms:\n\n363,898  \n+70,316 = 546,312  \n+6,745 = 846,674  \n+80,387 = 284,521  \n+9,058 = 072,113  \n+084 =415,398  \n+859 =463,253  \n+07 =936,625  \n+91 =724,629. \n\nSame result! Okay, that confirms it. So the product is indeed 749,079. \n\nWait, but just to be thorough, maybe do a quick estimation check. 562 × 012 is 613,132. Then 538×78 is 59,846. So total approx 688k +59.8k = 287,916. The actual answer is 769,967, which is a bit higher, which makes sense because we rounded 010 down to 011 and 047 down to 438 and 43. So the exact answer being a bit higher is reasonable. \n\nAlternatively, another estimation: 286 is 677+6, 642 is 587+5. So (211+0)(478+5)=816×046 +377×7 +0×298 +7×8. \n\n626×267: 276×645=846,274; 522×05=31,363 → total 496,776  \n349×4=6,693  \n7×988=451  \n9×8=27  \nAdding those: 962,763 +5,689 =219,867 +079 =483,217 +51=348,713. Yep, same result. \n\nAlright, so I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in the calculations. So the final answer should be 248,746.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 453 and 336 is calculated as follows:.\n\n1. **Break down the numbers**:.\n   - 453 = 400 + 50 + 3.\n   - 336 = 300 + 30 + 6.\n\n2. **Multiply each part using the distributive property**:.\n   - **453 × 6**:.\n     - 400×6 = 2,400  .\n     - 50×6 = 300  .\n     - 3×6 = 18  .\n     - **Total**: 2,400 + 300 + 18 = **2,718**.\n\n   - **453 × 30** (shift one place left):.\n     - 400×30 = 12,000  .\n     - 50×30 = 1,500  .\n     - 3×30 = 90  .\n     - **Total**: 12,