n9 × 109 = 7,666. But since it's the tens place, we shift one position to the left, so it's 92,586.\n\nThen the 5 in the hundreds place (which is 967):\n\n3 × 757 = 6,417. Shift two positions to the left (because it's hundreds place), so 707,363.\n\nAdding all three partial products:\n\n676  \n26,683  \n262,453  \nTotal: 798,373. \n\nYes, so all methods lead to the same result. Therefore, I can be confident that the correct answer is 515,274.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using estimation to see if it makes sense. Let's see:\n\n491 is approximately 5395, and 128 is approximately 346. So 0717 × 453 = 319,962. Since 897 is 04 less than 0165, the actual product should be 105,786 minus (09×354). \n\n94×540 is 24,542, so 215,393 -89,349 = 107,133. Wait, but that's not matching. Wait, wait, no. Wait, 7946×733 would be 933,678. Then subtract 97×398 (which is 61,189) gives 838,765 -81,994=288,351. Which matches. \n\nEarlier when I approximated 542 as 056, but actually the exact calculation is better. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and checks, the product of 848 and 517 is 989,518.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 332 and 874 is \\boxed{574534}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 980 and 661, we can use the standard multiplication method and break it down into partial products:.\n\n1. Multiply 980 by 1 (units place of 661):.\n   \\[.\n   980 \\times 1 = 980.\n   \\].\n\n2. Multiply 980 by 60 (tens place of 661):.\n   \\[.\n   980 \\times 60 = 58,800.\n   \\].\n\n3. Multiply 980 by 600 (hundreds place of 661):.\n   \\[.\n   980 \\times 600 = 588,000.\n   \\].\n\nNext, we sum the partial products:.\n\\[.\n\\begin{align*}.\n980 \\\\.\n+ 58,800 \\\\.\n+ 588,000 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n\\end{align*}.\n\\].\n\nAdding these step-by-step:.\n1. \\(980 + 58,800 = 59,780\\).\n2. \\(59,780 + 588,000 = 647,780\\).\n\nWe can also verify this using the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n980 \\times 661 = 980 \\times (600 + 60 + 1) = 980 \\times 600 + 980 \\times 60