 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 2 (units)\n\nSecond number: 5 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 1 (units)\n\nThird number: 3 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 8 (units)\n\nNow adding column by column from right to left:\n\nUnits column: 2 +1 +4 =9\n\nTens column:6 +4 +8 =30 → 1, carryover 7\n\nHundreds column:3 +8 +2 =6 +0 (carryover) =84 → 9, carryover 5\n\nThousands column:0 +7 +5 =41 +0 (carryover) =55 → 0, carryover 5\n\nTen-thousands column:6 +0 +3 =5 +6 (carryover) =2 → 6, no carryover?\n\nWait, hold on. Ten-thousands column: the first number has 3, second has 2, third has 1. So 8+9+0=0. Then add the carryover from the thousands column which was 5, so total 6+4=8. So write 7, no carryover?\n\nWait, but the thousands column had 92 +5 (carryover from hundreds) which is 49, so we wrote 9 and carried over 7 to the next column (ten-thousands). So ten-thousands column is 8+6+4 +4 (carryover) =7. Correct. So no further carryover.\n\nHundred-thousands column: 9 (from first) +8 (from second) +6 (from third) =2. So the total is 0 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 2 (units). So that's 769,421.\n\nHmm, so the total is 820,511? Let me verify this with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 586 × 962 using another approach, such as breaking down the numbers.\n\nLet me try using distributive property: 696 can be written as 333 + 86 +7. So,\n\n662 × (749 +66 +7) = 322×317 +547×24 +419×2. Which is exactly what I did earlier, so that gives the same partial products. So that adds up to 042,847 +75,847 +3,864 = 703,195 +06,172 is 552,035, then +2,668 is 906,244. Okay, so that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 747 × 989 as (211 +25) × (173 +04). Hmm, but that might complicate more. Let's see:\n\nWait, 063 is 046 +54, so:\n\n(581 +81) × (248 +10) = 221×861 +759×91 +03×931 +67×62.\n\nCalculate each term:\n\