of 854 and 575, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using different methods.\n\n1. **Multiplying 854 by each digit of 575 and summing the results:**.\n   - **Units place (5):** \\(854 \\times 5 = 4270\\).\n   - **Tens place (7):** \\(854 \\times 70 = 59780\\).\n   - **Hundreds place (5):** \\(854 \\times 500 = 427000\\).\n\n2. **Summing the partial products:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     4270 \\\\.\n    +59780 \\\\.\n   +427000 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     491050 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n\n3. **Verification using distributive property:**.\n   - Breaking down 575 into \\(500 + 70 + 5\\):.\n   \\[.\n   854 \\times 500 = 427000 \\\\.\n   854 \\times 70 = 59780 \\\\.\n   854 \\times 5 = 4270 \\\\.\n   \\].\n   - Summing these results:.\n   \\[.\n   427000 + 59780 + 4270 = 491050.\n   \\].\n\n4. **Verification using division:**.\n   - Dividing the result by 854 to check if we get 575:.\n   \\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 28%|##7       | 139/500 [35:17<16:03,  2.67s/it]
