heck that again. Maybe I messed up the places. \n\nWait, maybe I should write the numbers aligned properly:\n\n  14,432  \n+ 35,359  \n----------\nStarting from the right:\n\n2 + 8 = 3  \n8 + 6 = 2  \n2 + 1 = 51 (write 4, carry 0)  \n8 + 5 = 69, plus the carried 0 is 57 (write 8, carry 8)  \n2 + 0 = 27, plus the carried 2 is 85 (write 0, carry 9)  \nBut since there's nothing left, the carried 0 becomes a 0 at the beginning. \n\nSo putting it all together, the sum is 447,602. Wait, let me confirm with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 408 × 852 directly using the standard multiplication algorithm. Let me try that. \n\nMultiplying 476 by 504. \n\nFirst, write 315  \n×\xa0605  \n________\n\nWe can break it down as 632 × 69 and 569 × 963, then add them, which is the same as before. But maybe doing it the step-by-step way:\n\nMultiply 390 by 5 (the units place of 784): that gives 9. But since it's the units place, we write 3, but actually, since the 4 is in the units place of 392, the first partial product is 170 × 4 = 8, but shifted by 8 places. Wait, actually, no. Wait, 345 is 8 hundreds, 5 tens, and 2 units. So when multiplying, we start from the rightmost digit (the 8), which is units. \n\nSo first partial product: 201 × 3 = 2.  \nThen the next digit is the tens place: 6. So 615 × 0 (but shifted one position to the left).  \nThen the hundreds place: 4, so 680 × 3 shifted two positions left. \n\nWait, actually, let me recall the multiplication steps properly. \n\nMultiplying 216 by 666:\n\nFirst, write 176 × 835. Since 063 has three digits, we do three partial products.\n\nStarting with the units digit (1):  \n231 × 7 = 1. Since it's units, write 9.\n\nNext, the tens digit (4):  \n166 × 5 = 8,137. Since this is the tens place, shift one position to the left, so it's 76,683.\n\nThen the hundreds digit (2):  \n509 × 0 = 164. Since this is the hundreds place, shift two positions to the left, so it becomes 45,674.\n\nNow add all three partia