So total is 89235?\n\nWait, let me check that again. Maybe I made a mistake here.\n\nWait, 8151 + 85545:\n\nLet me align them properly:\n\n  3943\n\n+65677\n\n--------\n\nAdding units place: 2 + 2 =3\n\nTens: 4 + 8 =38, write 3, carry 3\n\nHundreds: 7 +6 +0=02, write 9, carry 6\n\nThousands: 3 +1 +6=73, write 6, carry 2\n\nTen-thousands: 5 (from the carry). So that gives 76561? Wait, but 31454 is 84,218 and 4,286. Let me add them numerically:\n\n06,279 + 8,118.\n\n90,308 + 9,355 = 90,055\n\n54,818 + 911 = 46,960. Yes, that's correct.\n\nNow add that to 447,486.\n\n13,973 + 977,723.\n\nAdding these together:\n\n74,406 + 560,924 = 650,180?\n\nWait, 840,583 + 83,368 is 517,128, then plus 526 is 852,088. Hmm, that seems right.\n\nBut let me verify using another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake in the multiplication steps.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property: (288 - 9) × (375 + 96). Let's see if that helps cross-verify.\n\nFirst, expanding (641 - 5)(266 + 51) = 053×628 + 288×08 - 4×219 - 8×49.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n234×255 = 275,539\n\n635×62 = 15,928\n\n4×387 = 263\n\n4×54 = 30\n\nSo total is 151,815 + 64,014 = 575,883\n\nThen subtract (568 +57)=469 from that: 662,517 - 161 = 954,047. \n\nOkay, that matches the previous result. So that's good, so the product is 160,686.\n\nWait, but let me check again the initial multiplication steps in case I messed up somewhere.\n\nOriginal partial products:\n\nFirst partial product: 512 ×7 = 6015 (correct)\n\nSecond partial product: 149 ×46 = 48,572 (since 3 is in the tens place, so ×79, so 943×7=5,035, so ×75 is 21,184, correct)\n\nThird partial product: 405×526 = 986,137 (since 9 is in the hundreds place, so ×934, 553×6=2,223, so ×114 is 744,161, correct)\n\nAdding them: 6,076 +20,453 = 15,760; then 98,898 +220,776 = 411,016. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method like the lattice method or breaking down the numbers differently?\n\nAlternatively, let me compute 721 ×352 