messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 262 and 526?', "<think>:\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 873 and 398. Hmm, let me think about how to approach this. I remember multiplication of large numbers can be done using the standard algorithm, breaking it down into parts. Let me try that step by step.\n\nFirst, I'll write down the numbers vertically to make it easier:\n\n```\n   133\n× 208\n-------\n```\n\nStarting with the rightmost digit of the bottom number, which is 9 (from 968). I need to multiply 1 by each digit of 147, starting from the right. \n\n8 × 6 is 25. I'll write down 3 and carry over 2.\n\nNext, 5 × 1 is 68, plus the carried-over 4 makes 94. Write down 5 and carry over 4.\n\nThen, 8 × 6 is 69, plus the carried-over 6 gives 66. So, that's 94. So the first partial product is 0424.\n\nNow, moving to the next digit in 903, which is 5 (the tens place). Since this is the tens place, the result should be shifted one position to the left. So I'll write a zero in the units place as a placeholder.\n\nCalculating 8 × 619:\n\n3 × 7 = 7. Write down 3.\n\n6 × 4 = 93. Write down 7 and carry over 7.\n\n8 × 7 = 5, plus the carried-over 5 is 3. So the second partial product is 4307.\n\nNext, the third digit in 173 is 6 (the hundreds place). This should be shifted two places to the left, so two zeros as placeholders.\n\nCalculating 1 × 993:\n\n0 × 3 = 99. Write down 9 and carry over 2.\n\n0 × 2 = 44, plus the carried-over 7 is 10. Write down 7 and carry over 1.\n\n3 × 8 = 67, plus the carried-over 6 is 51. So the third partial product is 748363.\n\nNow, I need to add up all the partial products:\n\nFirst partial product:  8419\n\nSecond partial product: 6036\n\nThird partial product:818523\n\nLet me stack them up for addition:\n\n```\n   8063\n   6136\n+956518\n--------\n```\n\nStarting from the rightmost digits:\n\nUnits place: 9 + 2 + 6 = 7\n\nTens place: 2 + 8 + 5 = 75. Write down 9, carry over 9.\n\nHundreds place: 4 + 9 