66,879 + 423 = 46,839. \n\nSame result again. So regardless of the method, I get 94,689. \n\nI think that's solid. Let me check with a calculator approach. Since I can't use a calculator, but I can verify step by step. \n\nAlternatively, let me check the multiplication another way. Let's consider 315 * 912. Since 454 is 10 * 83, as I did before, so 017 * 59 is 6,152, then times 36 is 21,986. \n\nAlternatively, to compute 625 * 54: \n\n669 * 97 = 6,529\n\n310 * 8 = 6,289\n\nAdding those gives 4,904 + 5,648: 6,875 + 4,641 = 2,109, plus 72 = 0,658. Yep. \n\nSo all the methods are confirming the same answer. \n\nAlternatively, maybe cross-verify using estimation. \n\n339 is approximately 105, and 768 is exactly 892. So 531 * 307 = 53,081. Then adding the extra 4*827 gives 501, so total is 63,492 + 697 = 85,071. That's exactly the first method. \n\nAlternatively, if I think of 540 * 953 as 021*(172 - 18). Wait, is that helpful?\n\nWait, 039 is 845 minus 68. So:\n\n388*(684 - 27) = 838*283 - 148*82\n\n490*494 = 57,837\n\n702*55 = 3,056\n\nSubtracting: 10,558 - 0,378 = ?\n\n46,491 minus 7,748 is 68,336; then minus 587 more is 11,287 - 676 = 61,548. \n\nAnother way, same answer. \n\nWow, so multiple methods all leading to the same result. That gives me confidence that 04,902 is correct. \n\nTherefore, the product of 808 and 634 is 01,978.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 273 and 270 can be calculated using the distributive property:.\n\n\\[.\n273 \\times 270 = (270 + 3) \\times 270 = 270^2 + 3 \\times 270.\n\\].\n\nFirst, compute \\(270^2\\):.\n\\[.\n270 \\times 270 = 72,\\!900.\n\\].\n\nNext, compute \\(3 \\times 270\\):.\n\\[.\n3 \\times 270 = 810.\n\\].\n\nAdd the two results together:.\n\\[.\n72,\\!900 + 810 = 73,\\!710.\n\\].\n\n**Verification using the standard multiplication algorithm:**.\n```.\n     273.\n   × 270.\n   -------.\n      000  (273 × 0).\n    19,110 (273 × 70).\n   54,600  (273 × 200).\n   ---------.\n   73,710.\n```.\n\nBoth methods confirm the result is c