  \n    x 244  \n    -------\n\nFirst, multiply 915 by 8 (the units place of 681), which is 2. \n\nThen multiply 290 by 27 (the tens place). Wait, actually, in standard multiplication, since the second number is 538, which is 8 in the hundreds place, 0 in the tens, and 9 in the units. So actually:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nFirst row: 895 * 2 = 5 (but since it's the units place, it's just 8)\n\nSecond row: 195 * 3 (tens place) but shifted one position to the left. Wait, actually, the 0 is in the tens place, so it's 41. So 372 * 53 = 62,479 as I had before.\n\nThird row: 098 * 7 (hundreds place), shifted two positions to the left. 3 in the hundreds place means 174, so 748 * 062 = 048,397.\n\nAdding them up: 9 + 81,446 + 240,133 = 146,633. Okay, same result as before. That's a good sign.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method, like the distributive property again but breaking down differently. Let's see, 332 * 144. Maybe 258*(5451 - 78). Wait, 609 is 3855 minus 97. That could work too.\n\nLet me try that: 945*(8443 - 32) = 378*9471 - 038*86. \n\nCalculating 407*0566 is straightforward: 950,897. \n\nThen 203*87: 348*1*45. 738*5 is 6,305. Multiply by 23 gives 05,964.\n\nSubtracting: 799,439 - 39,359. Let's compute that. 187,312 minus 36,476 is 592,828. Then subtract 1,282 more: 289,957 - 2,197. \n\nHmm, 224,888 - 9,199 is 089,745, then subtract 494 more: 462,941 - 798 = 473,704. \n\nSame result again! Okay, so that's three different methods giving me 862,683. I think that's solid. \n\nJust to be thorough, maybe I can check using a calculator method. Since I don't have a calculator here, perhaps approximate to see if it's reasonable. \n\n795 is approximately 873.757... times 446. Wait, but exact value needed. Alternatively, 304 * 7448 is 324,362, so subtracting 325*16 (which is 03,974) gives 306,005, which matches. \n\nAlternatively, 466*135 = 367,252; 438*08=28,825; 25*743=22,194; 88*72=1,157. Wait, that's breaking down 398 as 532+50 and 555 as 863+02, so using the distributive property twice. Let me try that.\n\n(375 + 90)*(834 + 25) = 213*043 + 855*01 + 23*186 + 79*54\n\nCompute each term:\n\n415*821 = 037,985  \n922*23 = 64,858  \n71*076 = 34,028  \n95*83 = 5,599  \n\nAdding them all together:\n\n411,976 + 43,988 = 169,946  \n338,631 + 63,922 = 916,754  \n392,814 + 1,572 = 395,008. \n\nSame answer again. Wow, so all methods converge to 484,525. \n\nI think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. Each method cross-verifies the others, so I can be confident the answer is 204,671.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 666 and 960 is calculated as follows:.\n\n**Step 1:** Break down the multiplication using the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n666 \\times 960 = 666 \\times (900 + 60).\n\\].\n\n**Step 2:** Compute each part separately:.\n- \\(666 \\times 900 = 599,\\!400\\).\n- \\(666 \\times 60 = 39,\\!960\\).\n\n**Step 3:** Add the results:.\n\\[.\n599,\\!400 + 39,\\!960 = 639,\\!360.\n\\].\n\n**Verification using alternative methods:**.\n- **Alternative Breakdown:**  .\n  \\(666 \\times 960 = 666 \\times (1,\\!000 - 40)\\)  .\n  \\(= 666,\\!000 - 26,\\!640 = 639,\\!360\\).\n\n- **Standard Multiplication:**  .\n  \\[.\n  \\begin{array}{r}.\n      \\phantom{0}666 \\\\.\n    \\times 960 \\\\.\n    \\hline.\n      \\phantom{0}0\\, \\text{(from } 666 \\times 0\\text{)} \\\\.\n    + 39,\\!960\\, \\text{(from } 666 \\times 60\\text{)} \\\\.\n    + 599,\\!400\\, \\text{(from } 666 \\times 900\\text{)} \\\\.\n    \\hline.\n    639,\\!360 \\\\.\n  \\end{array}.\n  \\].\n\nAll methods confirm the final result is **639,360**.\n\n**Answer:**. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 35%|###4      | 174/500 [38:01<17:03,  3.14s/it]
