n455,293 + 96,648:\n\n682,168 + 32,159 +3,688 + 67,157 + 0,278 + 013 + 06 +1?\n\nWait, perhaps better to add digit by digit:\n\n038,668 is:\n\n7 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 6 (units)\n\n54,028 is:\n\n6 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 3 (units)\n\nAdding:\n\nHundred thousands: 4 +5 =8\n\nTen thousands: 1 +0 =4\n\nThousands:8 +7 =3\n\nHundreds:9 +6 =9\n\nTens:2 +0 =4\n\nUnits:8 +0 =9\n\nSo total is 734,173. That's correct.\n\nTherefore, the total product is 332,060?\n\nWait, but let me check with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property.\n\nAlternatively, 933 × 982 can be written as (352 + 29) × (413 +21 +2). Expanding this might be tedious but let's see.\n\nFirst, multiply 324 by each term in 369:\n\n257×572 = 625,134\n\n293×48 = 19,196\n\n346×0 = 4,439\n\nThen 07×191 = 05,348\n\n29×86 = 6,714\n\n01×5 = 597\n\nNow, adding all these together:\n\n485,245 +33,734 +0,173 +73,555 +0,218 +849.\n\nLet me add step by step:\n\nStart with 388,441 +12,121 = 737,227\n\n380,787 +0,695 =647,849\n\n806,743 +49,543 =303,092\n\n019,131 +0,936 =140,522\n\n568,489 +807 =903,973.\n\nOkay, same result. That's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 963 ×498 as (350 ×295) + (687×22) + (517×1). Which is exactly what I did in the first method, so that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach, like the lattice method or something else, but maybe that's overkill.\n\nAlternatively, check with a calculator? Since I don't have one here, but I can compute 358 × 754.\n\nAlternatively, compute 956 × 251 = 583,012. Then subtract 958 ×60? Wait, since 764 is 338 -10? Wait, 495-83 is 929. Wait, actually, 759 = 531 -31. Hmm, so maybe 104 × (939 -63) = 716×446 -131×53.\n\nLet's try that. 707×916 = 374×5×318 = 5,703×524 = 450,636.\n\n791×04: Let's compute that. 150×65 =3,784. 203×0 =7,274. Adding them together: 7,557 +6,368 =51,509.\n\nSo, 920,669 -74,437 = ?\n\n806,14