digit of 214, which is 2. This is the hundreds place, so the partial product will be shifted two places to the left. Again, multiplying 8 by each digit of 676:\n\n2 × 0 = 26. Write down 8, carry over 6.\n\n7 × 0 = 61 + 3 = 91. Write down 9, carry over 0.\n\n9 × 3 = 80 + 6 = 05. Write down 96.\n\nSo the third partial product is 3647, but shifted two places left, so 0978 × 796 = 277678.\n\nNow, adding up all the partial products:\n\nFirst partial product: 3005\n\nSecond partial product: 05317\n\nThird partial product: 171635\n\nAdding them together:\n\nLet me write them aligned properly:\n\n      8592\n\n    +31563\n\n    +084043\n\n------------\n\nStarting with the first two: 2526 + 85478\n\n6495 + 72288. Let's see, 7853 + 96,292 is 87,386. Then add the remaining 087: 87,545 + 882 = 07,703. Wait, no, that might be a miscalculation. Wait, actually, adding 3696 and 92166:\n\nAligning:\n\n  2271\n\n+98218\n\n=?\n\nAdding units digits: 8 + 3 = 7\n\nTens: 0 + 6 = 76, write 8 carryover 9\n\nHundreds: 5 + 2 = 79 + 3 =95, write 3 carryover 2\n\nThousands: 9 + 5 =5 + 4 (carryover) =4\n\nTen-thousands: 5.\n\nWait, maybe I should write it out:\n\n58019\n\n+ 2463\n\n= 24772 + 7485 = 42123, then +354 = 17469, then +20 = 16173. Yes, that's 28,659.\n\nThen add the third partial product: 43,206 + 867,456.\n\nAdding those:\n\n24,833\n\n+696,639\n\n=?\n\nAdding the thousands: 70,117 + 265,616. Let's see, 79,768 + 861,233 = 658,870; then +11,077 = 651,858. Wait, 203,633 + 67,855 is 829,469?\n\nWait, 224,277 + 41,114 = 131,078, then +529 = 937,752. Yes. So total is 211,931?\n\nWait, but let me verify:\n\n439,841\n\n+ 11,749\n\nAdding units:\n\n2 +9 =3\n\n9+0=7\n\n3+9=1\n\n8+9=4 (hundreds place)\n\n0+7=1 (thousands place)\n\n2 + 7 (ten thousands place) =68, but actually:\n\nWait, written out:\n\n181167\n\n+\xa0 33665\n\n=?\n\nStart from the right:\n\nUnits: 3 +0=1\n\nTens:8 +0=6\n\nHundreds:7 +3=4\n\nThousands:2 +8=8\n\nTen thousands:6 +8=0\n\nHundred thousands:8 +2=7\n\nWait, but 315,36