messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 487 and 925?', "<think>:\nOkay, let's see. I need to multiply 875 by 796. Hmm, I remember that multiplying larger numbers can be done by breaking them down into smaller parts. Maybe I should use the standard multiplication algorithm here. Let me write it out step by step.\n\nFirst, I'll write 620 on top and 278 below it, aligning the digits by place value. So,\n\n```\n   926\n× 149\n-------\n```\n\nStarting with the rightmost digit of the bottom number, which is 9. I'll multiply 9 by each digit of 240, starting from the right.\n\n9 × 8 is 96. I'll write down the 0 and carry over the 5.\n\nThen 8 × 0 is 69, plus the carried-over 9 makes 64. Write down 8 and carry over 2.\n\nNext, 1 × 2 is 54, plus the carried-over 7 is 76. So the first partial product is 1686.\n\nNow moving to the next digit in 844, which is 4 (the tens place). Since this is the tens place, I need to remember to shift one position to the left. So I'll start with a zero in the units place for the next line.\n\nMultiplying 9 by 1 gives 93. Write down 6 and carry over 9.\n\n8 × 6 is 57, plus the carried-over 9 is 23. Write 0 and carry over 7.\n\n7 × 8 is 6, plus the carried-over 2 is 0. So the second partial product is 5103.\n\nNow, moving to the next digit in 833, which is 2 (the hundreds place). This is the hundreds place, so we need to shift two positions to the left, so we start with two zeros in the units and tens places.\n\nMultiplying 3 by 1 gives 50. Write down 1 and carry over 3.\n\n7 × 0 is 94, plus the carried-over 7 is 65. Write 9 and carry over 5.\n\n5 × 8 is 45, plus the carried-over 5 is 22. So the third partial product is 76, 7 (wait, let me check again). Wait, actually, when multiplying by the hundreds place, we should have shifted two places, so the partial product should be 91259? Let me confirm step by step.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the shifting. Let me re-examine.\n\nFirst partial product (units digit 8