n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 854 and 338 is \\boxed{265867}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 707 and 692, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using the distributive property and another method involving breaking down the numbers.\n\n### Standard Multiplication Algorithm:.\n1. Multiply 707 by 2 (units place):.\n   \\[.\n   707 \\times 2 = 1,414.\n   \\].\n2. Multiply 707 by 90 (tens place):.\n   \\[.\n   707 \\times 9 = 6,363 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 63,630.\n   \\].\n3. Multiply 707 by 600 (hundreds place):.\n   \\[.\n   707 \\times 6 = 4,242 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 424,200.\n   \\].\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications:.\n   \\[.\n   1,414 + 63,630 = 65,044.\n   \\].\n   \\[.\n   65,044 + 424,200 = 489,244.\n   \\].\n\n### Distributive Property:.\nBreak down the numbers into their place values:.\n\\[.\n(700 + 7) \\times (600 + 90 + 2).\n\\].\nExpand using the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n700 \\times 600 + 700 \\times 90 + 700 \\times 2 + 7 \\times 600 + 7 \\times 90 + 7 \\times 2.\n\\].\nCalculate each term:.\n\\[.\n700 \\times 600 = 420,000.\n\\].\n\\[.\n700 \\times 90 = 63,000.\n\\].\n\\[.\n700 \\times 2 = 1,400.\n\\].\n\\[.\n7 \\times 600 = 4,200.\n\\].\n\\[.\n7 \\times 90 = 630.\n\\].\n\\[.\n7 \\times 2 = 14.\n\\].\nSum all terms:.\n\\[.\n420,000 + 63,000 + 1,400 + 4,200 + 630 + 14 = 489,244.\n\\].\n\n### Verification Using Difference of Squares:.\nExpress 707 and 692 as:.\n\\[.\n707 = 700 + 7 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 692 = 700 - 8.\n\\].\nUse the formula \\((a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2\\) adjusted for the extra terms:.\n\\[.\n(700 + 7)(700 - 8) = 700^2 + 7 \\times 700 - 8 \\times 700 - 7 \\times 8.\n\\].\nCalculate each term:.\n\\[.\n700^2 = 490,000.\n\\].\n\\[.\n7 \\times 700 = 4,900.\n\\].\n\\[.\n-8 \\times 700 = -5,600.\n\\].\n\\[.\n-7 \\times 8 = -56.\n\\].\nSum all terms:.\n\\[.\n490,000 + 4,900 - 5,600 - 56 = 489,244.\n\\].\n\n### Final Answer. Therefore, my final answer is: