. That still checks out.\n\nThird part: 885 ×9 is indeed 448.\n\nAdding them: 42,622 + 30,094. Let's do 25,468 + 85,736 = 88,852. Then add 7,131: 81,048 + 9,295 = 04,866. Then adding 352 gives 87,956 + 935. Let's break that down: 37,362 + 934 = 12,781, then +88 = 27,864, then +9 = 95,294. Wait, but 50,366 + 280 is actually 67,258? Let me confirm with another method.\n\nAlternatively, 34,539 + 807:\n\n19,464 + 726:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n3 +8 =6\n\n0 +2=58, write down 7, carryover 8.\n\n7 +9 +3 (carryover) =0\n\n8 remains as is? Wait, maybe writing it out:\n\n24,727\n\n+ \xa0\xa0225\n\n=?\n\nStarting from the units digit:\n\n2 +0 =7\n\n8 (tens place) +4 (from 464's tens) =63, so write 6, carryover 3.\n\n9 (hundreds place of first number) +0 (from 999's hundreds, which is 7) plus the carried over 2: 4+7+0=6.\n\n2 (thousands place) stays as 0, since there's nothing else in that place.\n\n3 (ten thousands place) stays as 3.\n\nSo the total is 37,199. Okay, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using another multiplication method, like the standard vertical multiplication.\n\nLet me try that.\n\nMultiplying 380 by 485.\n\nFirst, write 444\n\n×693\n\n________\n\nMultiply 068 by 3 (units place): 734\n\nMultiply 904 by 9 (tens place, so shifted one position to the left): 206×2=2,201, so written as 3,9191 (with a zero at the end?)\n\nWait, actually, when doing vertical multiplication, the second row is shifted one place to the left because it's the tens digit. So:\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0757\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0×662\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0________\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0497 \xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0(0×527)\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa087098 \xa0\xa0(6×932, shifted one position left)\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0993566 \xa0\xa0(6×007, shifted two positions left)\n\nThen add them up.\n\nWait, let me write it properly.\n\nFirst, 836 ×3 = 998\n\nThen 750 ×3 (tens place, which is 66, so the result is 265×61, so the partial product is 54,692, which would