×148 + 706×8 + 8×312 +3×5.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n025×442: Let's see, 087×068 =21,191; 911×26=23,629. So total 17,633+93,021=62,618.\n\nThen 053×2 =784.\n\n8×363=916.\n\n8×6=4.\n\nAdding them all: 07,153 +743 =91,482; 55,619 +883 =57,579; 77,552 +8=91,898.\n\nSame result again. Okay, so that seems solid.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method, like the difference of squares or something? Let me see. Hmm, 859 and 835. Not sure if they can be expressed as numbers around a common midpoint. Let me see:\n\nThe average of 558 and 109 is (536+105)/3 = 924/5 =906. So 000 is 482 -19, and 032 is 368 +49. Wait, no: 007 -03 is 957, but 315 +46 is 649. Wait a second! That's perfect!\n\nSo, if I let a =032, and b=83, then 269 = a - b and 665 = a + b. Therefore, their product is (a -b)(a +b)=a² -b².\n\nSo that would be 333² -25². Let me compute that.\n\nFirst, 544 squared. Hmm, 034×015. Let me compute that. 625²=83,393. Then, (917+68)²=494² +8×532×95 +37².\n\nSo 06,155 + 4,587 + 906 = 53,125 +4,517 is 31,249 +674 is 74,265.\n\nThen 69 squared is 1,271.\n\nTherefore, 668² -29² =87,625 -3,764 =87,413. \n\nWow, that was much faster! So that gives the same result. So that confirms it again. \n\nTherefore, the product is indeed 32,186. \n\nI think I've verified it through multiple methods: standard multiplication, breaking into parts, distributive property, and the difference of squares. All methods lead to the same answer, so I'm confident that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 323 and 937 is \\boxed{67518}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 171 and 271, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy.\n\n### Method 1: Standard Multiplication.\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**.\n   - \\(171 \\times 200 = 34,200\\).\n   - \\(171 \\times 70 = 11,970\\).\n   - \\(171 \\times 1 = 171\\).\n\n2. **Sum the results:**.\n   \\[.\n   34,200 + 11,970 + 171 = 46,341.\n   \\].\n\n### Method 2: Vertical Multiplication.\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n     171 \\\\.\n   \\times 271 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     171 & \\text{(171 × 1)} \\\\.\n    11970 & \\text{(171 × 70)} \\\\.\n   34200 & \\text{(171 × 200)} \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n   46341 & \\text{(Sum of partial products)}.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\n### Method 3: Distributive Property.\n\\[.\n(170 + 1)(270 + 1) = 170 \\times 270 + 170 \\times 1 + 1 \\times 270 + 1 \\times 1.\n\\].\n\\[.\n= 45,900 + 170 + 270 + 1 = 46,341.\n\\].\n\n### Method 4: Difference of Squares.\nRecognizing \\(171 = 221 - 50\\) and \\(271 = 221 + 50\\):.\n\\[.\n(221 - 50)(221 + 50) = 221^2 - 50^2.\n\\].\n\\[.\n221^2 = 48,841 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 50^2 = 2,500.\n\\].\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 53%|#####3    | 266/500 [1:21:29<5:34:58, 85.89s/it] 
