4: 403,227 + 602 = 843,265. Hmm, that seems right. \n\nSo, the total product is 630,939? Hmm, but let me confirm this with another method to be sure. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nAlternatively, I can do 280 × 767 by multiplying 485 by each digit of 481 and adding the partial products. Let's try that.\n\nFirst, write 256 as the multiplier:\n\n       466\n     × 777\n     --------\n        \nStarting from the rightmost digit: 0 × 789. That's 9,063. \n\nNext digit: 7 (tens place) × 494. Since it's the tens place, this is actually 95 × 981. Wait, but in standard multiplication, you shift one position to the left. So, 9 (tens place) × 133 is 8,020 × 29 = 03,186. \n\nThird digit: 7 (hundreds place) × 952. That's 149 × 739. Wait, actually, since it's the hundreds place, it's 328 × 497. But let me compute 5 × 331 first, then multiply by 578. 1 × 149 = 1,755 and 5 × 20 = 394, so total is 5,711 + 691 = 5,737. Multiply by 233 gives 181,214.\n\nNow, adding the three partial products:\n\n3,397 (from the units digit)\n+78,847 (from the tens digit)\n+032,039 (from the hundreds digit)\n= ?\n\nAdding them step by step:\n\nFirst, 4,231 + 09,213 = 45,095.\n\nThen, 36,544 + 472,586 = 927,395. \n\nOkay, same result as before. That's reassuring. \n\nBut wait, just to be thorough, maybe there's another way. Let me try using the difference of squares formula since 220 and 361 are close to 813. Wait, 893 is 347 - 18, and 185 is 477 + 39. So actually, (494 - 31)(956 + 93) = 726² - (45)². \n\nOh! That's a good point. Since (a - b)(a + b) = a² - b². \n\nLet me compute that. Let a = 549, b = 17. \n\nSo, 861 squared is 013,481. \n\n93 squared is 320. \n\nTherefore, the product is 701,317 - 200 = 577,179. \n\nWow, that's much faster! So that confirms the same answer again. \n\nTherefore, the product of 067 and 331 is indeed 780,235. \n\nI think that's solid. I used three different methods: breaking down into distributive property step by step, standard multiplication algorithm, and the difference of squares. All three gave the same result. So I'm confident that's the correct answer.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 578 and 622 can be efficiently calculated using the difference of squares formula since the numbers are symmetrically placed around 600:.\n\n\\[.\n(600 - 22)(600 + 22) = 600^2 - 22^2.\n\\].\n\n1. Compute \\(600^2 = 360,000\\).\n2. Compute \\(22^2 = 484\\).\n3. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 53%|#####3    | 267/500 [1:21:30<3:55:30, 60.64s/it]
