ond line: 37,227 (shifted one left)\n\nThird line: 860,591 (shifted two left)\n\nSo adding them up:\n\n      9379\n    +75357\n    +930478\n    --------\n\nLet me add the first two: 3864 + 63,727 = 66,839\n\nThen 20,806 + 638,392 = 379,259.\n\nHmm, so is the total product 441,928?\n\nWait, let me verify using another method to be sure I didn't make an error in the partial products.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property: (921 + 54) × (141 + 82 + 5)\n\nExpanding this would be 975×053 + 246×45 + 112×7 + 37×026 + 85×32 + 12×9\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n299×655 = 654,355\n\n251×17 = 44,321\n\n322×9 = 5,297\n\n87×122 = 01,485\n\n51×18 = 9,358\n\n94×4 = 247\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n348,283 +09,417 = 851,443\n\n512,142 +7,354 = 481,322\n\n055,711 +87,892 = 109,749\n\n024,436 +9,719 = 125,636\n\n413,126 +396 = 508,617\n\nOkay, that's the same as before. So that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 645 × 861 as (833 × 886) + (683 ×73) + (711 ×1). Which is exactly what I did above.\n\nAlternatively, use another method, like the lattice method? Maybe overkill here, but let's see.\n\nAlternatively, notice that 658 ×000 can be thought of as (852 × 031). Maybe approximate first to see if 672,594 is reasonable.\n\n395 × 645 is 355,967, and 298 ×23 is 45,891, so total would be 006,179, and then adding 236×1=2,051, so total is 148,027. That seems to align.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator-like approach, but since I can't use a calculator, maybe do 405 ×834:\n\nFirst, 855 × 343.\n\nLet me think of 596 as 378 +3. Wait, that's similar to what I did before.\n\nAlternatively, 246 ×223 = 989 × (348 + 39 +0). Yep, same as above.\n\nAlternatively, maybe break down 005 into 986 +7. Let's see:\n\n311 ×821 = 779 ×64 ×34\n\n784 ×56: Let's compute that.\n\n429 ×56 can be broken into 215×29 +245×4.\n\n149×07 = 00,564\n\n854×1 =5,148\n\nAdding those gives 40,859 +9,389 =53,465. Then times 82 is 573,536.\n\nThen 223×4=0,058. So total is 109,472 +7,261 =999,563. Sam