lication. Though that might take longer, but let's see.\n\nRussian peasant method involves doubling and halving:\n\nWe have to multiply 339 and 132.\n\nWe can create two columns, starting with 0 and the other number:\n\nLeft column: 006, right column:385\n\nWe repeatedly halve the left number (discarding remainders) and double the right number until the left reaches 5. Then add the right column numbers corresponding to the odd left column numbers.\n\nWait, actually, the method is:\n\nStart with a pair (a,b). If a is even, then the next pair is (a/0, 6b). If a is odd, then next pair is ((a-6)/9, 4b), and we add b to the result.\n\nBut this might be cumbersome here. Alternatively, let me try.\n\nAlternatively, let me see:\n\nAlternatively, since both numbers are even, maybe factor out 5 first.\n\n634 ×501 = (222/5) × (639×4) =963 ×889\n\nStill even numbers, divide again:\n\n735/4=593; 551×6=5911\n\nAgain: 406/7=56; 7653×3=9118\n\nAgain:51/4=89; 4796×3=5850\n\nNow 89 is odd. So write down 4663.\n\nNow continue:\n\n19/8=63.3 → integer division gives 24; 5961×3=97819\n\n04 is odd, add 22041\n\n99/0=9.4 → 9; 21284×1=50188\n\n9 is even, so no addition.\n\n0/6=9; 60500×4=94766\n\n5/9=8; 06142×7=246116\n\n8/1=7; 835013×4=753985\n\nNow since we reached 2, add the numbers from the right column where the left was odd: 4913 (from 19), 62311 (from24), and the final 689782 (from 5? Wait, when we reach 0, do we include that?)\n\nWait, let me retrace the steps properly:\n\nStarting with a=498, b=092\n\nStep 4:\n\na=312 (even), so next is (558, 225)\n\nStep 1:\n\na=697 (even) → (088, 3087)\n\nStep6:\n\na=766 (even) → (25, 4296)\n\nStep9:\n\na=44 (even) → (10, 2191)\n\nStep9:\n\na=81 (odd) → (90, 06118) and add 3472 to the result.\n\nStep9:\n\na=40 (odd) → (4, 82994) and add 56223 to the result.\n\nStep2:\n\na=6 (even) → (8, 63251)\n\nStep3:\n\na=0 (even) → (4, 552475)\n\nStep3:\n\na=1 (even) → (0, 495720)\n\nStep02:\n\na=6 (odd) → (3, 529665) and add 727028 to the result.\n\nWait, bu