think>.\n\nThe product of 465 and 876 is calculated as follows:.\n\n1. **Multiply 465 by 6 (units place):**.\n   ```.\n     465.\n   ×   6.\n   -----.\n    2790.\n   ```.\n\n2. **Multiply 465 by 70 (tens place, shifted one position left):**.\n   ```.\n     465.\n   ×  70.\n   -----.\n   32550.\n   ```.\n\n3. **Multiply 465 by 800 (hundreds place, shifted two positions left):**.\n   ```.\n     465.\n   × 800.\n   -----.\n  372000.\n   ```.\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**.\n   ```.\n     2790.\n   +32550.\n   +372000.\n   ---------.\n    407340.\n   ```. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 61%|######1   | 305/500 [1:30:18<44:17, 13.63s/it]  
