es 897 = 200 \\times 897 + 10 \\times 897.\n   \\].\n   - Calculate \\(200 \\times 897\\):.\n     \\[.\n     200 \\times 897 = 2 \\times 100 \\times 897 = 2 \\times 897 \\times 100 = 1794 \\times 100 = 179400.\n     \\].\n   - Calculate \\(10 \\times 897\\):.\n     \\[.\n     10 \\times 897 = 8970.\n     \\].\n   - Add the results:.\n     \\[.\n     179400 + 8970 = 188370.\n     \\].\n\n2. **Using the standard multiplication algorithm:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n        210 \\\\.\n      \\times 897 \\\\.\n      \\hline.\n        1470 \\quad (\\text{210} \\times 7) \\\\.\n       1890 \\quad (\\text{210} \\times 90) \\\\.\n      168000 \\quad (\\text{210} \\times 800) \\\\.\n      \\hline.\n      188370 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   - Summing the partial products:.\n     \\[.\n     1470 + 18900 + 168000 = 188370.\n     \\].\n\n3. **Alternative method using distributive property:**.\n   \\[.\n   210 \\times 897 = 210 \\times (900 - 3) = 210 \\times 900 - 210 \\times 3.\n   \\].\n   - Calculate \\(210 \\times 900\\):.\n     \\[.\n     210 \\times 900 = 189000.\n     \\].\n   - Calculate \\(210 \\times 3\\):.\n     \\[.\n     210 \\times 3 = 630.\n     \\].\n   - Subtract the results:.\n     \\[.\n     189000 - 630 = 188370.\n     \\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 62%|######1   | 308/500 [1:31:08<51:09, 15.99s/it]
