32 + 594 is 348,433, then +00 is 615,462. Yes, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers:\n\n644,234  \n+\xa0 9,765  \n=?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 + 1 = 3  \n4 + 1 = 1  \n5 + 3 = 1  \n9 + 6 = 69 (carry over 5)  \n8 + 6 + 6 (carry) = 5  \nThe remaining digits: 9 and the carried over? Wait, maybe aligning them properly:\n\n498,515  \n\xa0\xa0 1,123  \n+________\n\nAligning:\n\n396964  \n\xa0 9493  \nSo adding:\n\nUnits place: 7 +5 =5  \nTens: 1 +7 =7  \nHundreds:4 +5=6  \nThousands:4 +5=29 (write 8, carry 0)  \nTen-thousands:0 + (carry 0)=4  \nHundred-thousands:0 remains\n\nWait, maybe I need to write it properly:\n\nLet me write them vertically:\n\n\xa0\xa0\xa0 421859  \n+\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa08974  \n——————\n\nStart from the rightmost digit:\n\n8 (units) + 1 =0  \n7 (tens) +6=5  \n2 (hundreds) +4=9  \n5 (thousands place): the first number has 2 in thousands place, the second has 5 in thousands place (since 1374 is 4 thousands, 8 hundreds, etc). Wait, actually, 2969 is:\n\nThousands place: 1  \nHundreds:1  \nTens:9  \nUnits:7\n\nWait, so the first number is 307,789:\n\nDigits: 5 (hundred thousands),0 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),8 (hundreds),3 (tens),9 (units)\n\nSecond number: 0 (thousands),0 (hundreds),6 (tens),4 (units). So when adding:\n\nStarting from units:\n\n8 +6=0  \n7 +9=4  \n9 (hundreds) +4 (hundreds)=6  \n7 (thousands) +5 (thousands)=75. So write 5 and carry over 8.  \n1 (ten thousands) + 2 (since second number has no ten thousands) + 2 (carry)=6  \n6 (hundred thousands) remains.\n\nSo the total is 958,054. Yes, that matches. Okay, so that's correct.\n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and checks, the product of 828 and 973 is 592,014.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 911 and 308 is calculated as follows:.\n\nFirst, break down 308 into 300 + 8:.\n\\[.\n911 \\times 308 = 911 \\times (300 + 8) = (911 \\times 300) + (911 \\times 8).\n\\].\n\nCalculate each part separately:.\n\\[.\n911 \\times 300 = 273,\\!300 \\quad \\text{(since } 911 \\times