th 3,077 + 68,019.\n\n0,729 + 81,839:\n\n6,150 + 52,565 = 59,845\n\n51,229 + 647 = 48,797\n\nSo that gives 31,000.\n\nNow add that to the third partial product: 87,235 + 922,562.\n\n80,422 + 368,056:\n\nAdding the thousands first: 33,271 + 939,344 = 569,146\n\nThen the remaining 532: 284,613 + 221 = 552,119.\n\nWait, hold on, that can't be right. Wait, 28,928 + 654,897.\n\nLet me do it digit by digit:\n\n426,083\n\n+\xa0 32,700\n\n= ?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n2 + 5 = 0\n\n5 +5 =1\n\n8 +2=71, write down 4 and carryover 3.\n\n8 +5 +8=99, write down 2, carryover 8.\n\n2 +0 +8=82, write down 9, carryover 3.\n\n8 + nothing +2=2.\n\nWait, let's write it out properly:\n\n791,458\n\n+\xa0 74,921\n\n------------\n\nStart from the rightmost digit:\n\nUnits place: 7 + 6 = 4\n\nTens place: 1 +1 =8\n\nHundreds place: 1 +4 =75. Write 4, carryover 7.\n\nThousands place: 0 (from 711,829) +5 (from 73,568) =78, plus the carried-over 0 makes 27. So write down 7, carryover 7.\n\nTen-thousands place: 2 (from 020,167) +7 (from 79,269) =3, plus the carried-over 0 makes 93. So write 8, carryover 4.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 6 (from 048,789) plus the carried-over 2 makes 5.\n\nSo putting it all together: 889,441?\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nWait 649,028 is:\n\n3 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 4 (units)\n\n67,331 is:\n\n4 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 9 (units)\n\nAdding:\n\nHundred thousands: 7 +9 =9\n\nTen thousands: 5 +5 =1\n\nThousands:9 +5 =85\n\nHundreds:7 +5=46\n\nTens:4 +2=6\n\nUnits:6 +8=4\n\nWait, but when adding step by step, the thousands place is 5 +9 =05, so we have to carry over 9 to the ten thousands place. But the ten thousands place was already 1 +0 =5, so adding the carried over 9 would make it 81. Wait, perhaps I need to do this more carefully.\n\nWait, let's use the standard addition method:\n\n       754,051\n\n     +\xa0 30,626\n\n     ------------\n\nStarting f