 14360\\).\n\n3. **Third partial product (359 × 800):**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     359 \\\\.\n   \\times \\ 800 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n   287200 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   - Calculate \\(359 \\times 8 = 2872\\), then shift two positions left: \\(2872 \\times 100 = 287200\\).\n\n4. **Summing the partial products:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     2513 \\\\.\n   + 14360 \\\\.\n   + 287200 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     304073 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   - \\(2513 + 14360 = 16873\\). Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 62%|######2   | 310/500 [1:31:14<29:59,  9.47s/it]
