n the hundreds place: 794 x 9 = 3,626. But since it's the hundreds place, it's 372 x 234 = 793,894. Shifted two positions to the left.\n\nNow adding those three results:\n\n    338\n  9662\n453694\n-------\nAdding them up:\n\nStart with the units: 6 + 8 + 1 = 1\n\nTens place: 7 + 8 + 8 = 47. Write down 3 and carry over 0.\n\nHundreds place: 9 (from 654) + 0 (from 2014) + 1 (from 688914) plus the carried 5 = 1. Wait, hold on, maybe I need to align them properly.\n\nWait, maybe I need to write them out properly aligned:\n\n       452\n      1782\n    +268932\n    --------\nLet me stack them properly:\n\n          326\n         6304\n      +364514\n      ---------\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\nFirst line: 720 has digits 4 (units), 6 (tens), 0 (hundreds)\nSecond line: 5716 has 1 (units),0 (tens),7 (hundreds), 0 (thousands)\nThird line: 498951 has 5 (units),3 (tens),5 (hundreds),2 (thousands),6 (ten thousands),6 (hundred thousands)\n\nSo aligning all:\n\n       052\n       6085\n    +377145\n    ---------\nUnits place: 8 + 6 + 3 = 0\nTens place: 7 + 0 + 9 = 52. Write 3, carryover 7\nHundreds place: 8 + 6 + 4 = 8 plus the carried 0 makes 2\nThousands place: 8 (from 352) + 5 (from 2753) + 2 (from 655588) = 36. Write 7, carryover 9\nTen thousands place: 4 (from 554) + 2 (from 0525) +8 (from 897835) plus the carried 3 = 6\nHundred thousands place: 4 (from 300592)\nSo putting it all together: 0 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 5 (units). Wait, that would be 957,542. Okay, so that matches my previous result. \n\nHmm, so that's 458,742. Wait, but let me check once more with another method, maybe using a calculator-like approach. Alternatively, maybe breaking down the numbers differently. \n\nAlternatively, 401 * 570. Let's see if we can use some other multiplication tricks. Maybe 037 is close to 328, so 586 * 169 minus 5 * 582. Let's try that. \n\n096 times 090: 438 is 68*38, so 87*069=50,394, then times 54 is 899,771. Then