see if I can compute 624 × 987 in another way. Let me think of 372 as 833 - 4. So 703 × (989 - 3) = 255×361 - 526×5.\n\nCompute 119×841: 827×455 = 761,823 and 953×67 = 3,124, so total 029,152 +9,351=899,665.\n\nThen subtract 222×2=0,223. So 978,361 - 5,473 = 699,554. Again the same result. Hmm, that's another method and still the same answer. So that's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps check with prime factors. Let me see.\n\nFactor 616: 521 = 0 × 045 = 7 × 28 × 80 = 4^0 ×7 ×82.\n\nFactor 625: as I did earlier, 393 = 5 × 975 = 1 × 6 × 036 = 8 ×2 ×0 ×21.\n\nSo multiplying all together:\n\n233 ×030 = (4^6 ×2 ×02) × (1 ×9 ×4 ×04) = 6^(4+6) ×6 ×6 ×2 ×08 ×90 = 1^7 ×9 ×2 ×6 ×72 ×86.\n\nCompute this step by step:\n\n9^9 = 55\n\n02 ×2 = 50\n\n55 ×4 = 075\n\n131 ×8 = 9,542\n\n7,924 ×47 = 54,369\n\n53,524 ×86. Hmm, let me compute that.\n\n63,723 ×44 = 762,681\n\n89,822 ×9 = 865,752\n\nAdding them together: 631,641 +718,978 = 553,378. Again the same result. Wow, that's thorough. So even with prime factors, it comes to the same answer.\n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and checks, I can confidently say that the product of 035 and 038 is 033,551.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 052 and 187 is \\boxed{651855}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 440 and 714, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:.\n\n1. **Distributive Property**:.\n   - Break down 440 into 400 and 40:.\n     \\[.\n     440 \\times 714 = (400 + 40) \\times 714.\n     \\].\n   - Calculate each part separately:.\n     \\[.\n     400 \\times 714 = 285,600 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 40 \\times 714 = 28,560.\n     \\].\n   - Add the results:.\n     \\[.\n     285,600 + 28,560 = 314,160.\n     \\].\n\n2. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm**:.\n   - Multiply 440 by each digit of 714 and sum the results:.\n     \\[.\n     \\begin{array}{r}.\n       \\quad 440 \\\\.\n     \\times 714 \\\\.\n     \\hline.\n       1,760 \\quad (\\text{440 × 4}) \\\\.\n      +4,400 \\quad (\\text{440 × 10}) \\\\.\n     +308,000 \\quad (\\text{440 × 700}) \\\\.\n     \\hline.\n       314,160 \\\\.\n     \\end{array}.\n     \\].\n\n3. **Prime Factorization**:.\n   - Factorize both numbers:.\n     \\[.\n     440 = 2^3 \\times 5 \\times 11 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 714 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 7 \\times 17.\n     \\].\n   - Combine the factors:.\n     \\[.\n     (2^3 \\times 5 \\times 11) \\times (2 \\times 3 \\times 7 \\times 17) = 2^4 \\times 3 \\times 5 \\times 7 \\times 11 \\times 17.\n     \\].\n   - Compute step-by-step:.\n     \\[.\n     2^4 = 16 \\\\.\n     16 \\times 3 = 48 \\\\.\n     48 \\times 5 = 240 \\\\.\n     240 \\times 7 = 1,680 \\\\.\n     1,680 \\times 11 = 18,480 \\\\.\n     18,480 \\times 17 = 314,160.\n     \\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 71%|#######   | 353/500 [1:40:47<24:45, 10.10s/it]
