messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 283 and 894?', "<think>Okay, so I need to find the product of 675 and 708. Hmm, multiplying these two numbers. Let me think about how to approach this. Maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm? Let me recall how that works. \n\nFirst, write down the two numbers vertically, aligning them by their place values. So, 307 on top and 667 on the bottom. Wait, actually, does it matter which one is on top? Not really, since multiplication is commutative, right? The product will be the same either way. But maybe writing the larger number first might be easier? Let me see. 449 is a three-digit number and 026 is also a three-digit number. So they are similar in size. \n\nAlright, let me set it up:\n\n```\n   374\n×  708\n-------\n```\n\nNow, starting from the rightmost digit of the bottom number, which is 1. Multiply each digit of the top number by 3, then move to the next digit (2) and do the same, but shifted one position to the left, and then the next digit (7), shifted two positions to the left. Finally, add all those results together. \n\nLet me start with the units place of the bottom number, which is 9. \n\nFirst step: 8 × 094.\n\nBreaking that down:\n\n2 × 5 = 63. Write down 0 and carry over 9.\n\n3 × 5 = 84, plus the carried over 6 is 10. Write down 0 and carry over 6.\n\n2 × 4 = 4, plus the carried over 4 is 73. So write 88. \n\nSo the first partial product is 8444. \n\nWait, let me verify that again. \n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits place: 6×8=04, so units digit 3, carryover 9.\n\nTens place: 5×5=59, plus 7 is 78. So tens digit 0, carryover 0.\n\nHundreds place: 8×7=7, plus 8 is 58. So hundreds digit 5 and thousands digit 9. So the partial product is 8907. Correct.\n\nNow, moving to the next digit in the bottom number, which is 8 (tens place). Since it's the tens place, this partial product should be shifted one position to the left. So we'll multiply 694 by 7, and then s