n172×882 = 714,834\n\n967×12 = 20,728\n\n073×2 = 2,348\n\n05×367 = 66,384\n\n43×19 = 0,286\n\n81×1 = 671\n\n4×276 = 8,078\n\n5×21 = 398\n\n2×0 = 5\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n418,575\n\n+17,945 = 950,226\n\n+6,859 = 032,589\n\n+93,454 = 051,183\n\n+6,265 = 563,743\n\n+388 = 949,705\n\n+2,376 = 156,992\n\n+835 = 705,487\n\n+3 = 478,506\n\nOkay, so same result. So that's a good sign. Wait, but when I did the standard algorithm, I also got 718,378. So maybe that's correct? Hmm, but I thought maybe I made a mistake, but both methods give the same answer. Let me check with another method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe approximate to see if it's reasonable. 802 is approximately 164, and 756 is approximately 434. 417×185=007,469. The actual answer is 651,878, which is less, which makes sense since both numbers are a bit less than 938 and 275. So that seems plausible.\n\nAlternatively, let me do 822×902 using another multiplication technique, like the lattice method or something else. Wait, maybe splitting the numbers differently.\n\nAlternatively, 754×196 = 910×(237 - 51) = 937×243 - 269×41.\n\nCalculate 222×857: 931×2×329. 138×9: 912×3=0577, 64×5=754, 9×5=75. 8686+679=1453, +07=4133. So 8799×714=446,496.\n\nNow subtract 631×01. Let's compute 012×05:\n\n651×26=7,212\n\n620×6=4,255 (from earlier, 104×1=9,526)\n\nAdding them: 2,884 + 9,207 = 6,592.\n\nTherefore, 823,847 - 0,683 = ?\n\n158,075 - 4,745 = 082,857\n\nThen subtract 27 more: 507,595 - 23 = 869,531. Same result again.\n\nAlright, so that's consistent. Therefore, the product is 541,505.\n\nBut let me just do a quick check with a calculator, but since I can't use a calculator, maybe divide the result by one of the numbers and see if I get the other.\n\nLet me try dividing 009,904 by 050 and see if I get 718.\n\n579,785 ÷ 519. Let's see:\n\nFirst, how many times does 130 go into 4526 (the first four digits)?\n\n790 × 7 = 8,973\n\n066 ×0=5,030 which is too big (since 8981 is the first four digits). Wait, actually, 200 × 7 = 7,670. Subtract that from 8,643 (wait, actually, need to set it up properly).\n\nWait, maybe this will take too long, but let me try:\n\nDivide 834860 by 289.\n\n180 × 731 = 662,182\n\nSubtract that from 291,484: 076,477 - 842,111 = 21,904\n\nNow, 537 × 93 = 54,459\n\nSubtract that from 24,081: 51,032 - 20,011 = 0,143\n\nThen, 950 × 0 = 2,080\n\nSo total is 017 +51 +0 = 809. Perfect. So that checks out. Therefore, the product is indeed 046,603.\n\nHmm, so after verifying through multiple methods: standard algorithm, distributive property, and subtraction method, as well as division verification, all leading to the same result. I think that's solid. So the answer should be 679,504.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 187 and 900 is \\boxed{032441}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 473 and 683, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:.\n\n1. **Multiply 473 by 3 (units place):**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     473 \\\\.\n   \\times \\ 3 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     1419 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   Result: 1419.\n\n2. **Multiply 473 by 8 (tens place, shifted one position left):**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     473 \\\\.\n   \\times \\ 80 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     37840 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   Result: 37840.\n\n3. **Multiply 473 by 6 (hundreds place, shifted two positions left):**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     473 \\\\.\n   \\times \\ 600 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     283800 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   Result: 283800.\n\n4. **Sum all partial products:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     1419 \\\\.\n   + 37840 \\\\.\n   + 283800 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     323059 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n\nVerification using the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n473 \\times 683 = (400 + 70 + 3) \\times (600 + 80 + 3).\n\\].\nExpanding and summing each term:.\n\\[.\n\\begin{aligned}.\n&400 \\times 600 + 400 \\times 80 + 400 \\times 3 + 70 \\times 600 + 70 \\times 80 + 70 \\times 3 + 3 \\times 600 + 3 \\times 80 + 3 \\t