tion to the left:**.\n   \\[.\n   103 \\times 9 = 927 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by one place becomes 9270)}.\n   \\].\n\n3. **Multiply 103 by 7 (the hundreds place of 794) and shift two positions to the left:**.\n   \\[.\n   103 \\times 7 = 721 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by two places becomes 72100)}.\n   \\].\n\n4. **Add the partial products:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     \\quad 412 \\\\.\n     +\\, 9270 \\\\.\n     +72100 \\\\.\n     \\hline.\n     81782 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n\nTo verify, we can use the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n103 \\times 794 = (100 + 3) \\times (700 + 90 + 4).\n\\].\nExpanding and summing the terms:.\n\\[.\n\\begin{aligned}.\n&100 \\times 700 + 100 \\times 90 + 100 \\times 4 \\\\.\n&+ 3 \\times 700 + 3 \\times 90 + 3 \\times 4 \\\\.\n&= 70000 + 9000 + 400 + 2100 + 270 + 12 \\\\.\n&= 70000 + 9000 + 400 + 2100 + 270 + 12 \\\\.\n&= 81782.\n\\end{aligned}.\n\\].\n\nAnother verification using the difference of squares approach:.\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 77%|#######6  | 383/500 [1:44:15<09:56,  5.10s/it]
