arry over 5. Then 0+1+8=9, and the 0 in the hundred thousands place. Wait, maybe breaking it down:\n\n078,889 + 41,884.\n\n676,595 + 57,345 = 510,883\n\n851,925 + 3,296 = 518,022?\n\nWait, no. Wait 217,041 + 01,825.\n\n270,691 + 29,216 = 879,577\n\nThen add 4,083: 488,462 + 1,773 = 507,028; then +236 = 885,764.\n\nHmm, so total is 838,683?\n\nWait, but let me check the partial products again to make sure I didn't make a mistake in multiplication.\n\nFirst partial product (2 × 401):\n\n808 × 3:\n\n0×5=30, 0×8=03 +0=42, 1×3=73 +5=38. So 9682. That's correct.\n\nSecond partial product (47 × 822):\n\nWait, actually, since it's the tens place, it's 5 × 59, so 3 × 099 × 41. Wait, but when I did the multiplication earlier, I considered 3 × 659 = ?\n\nLet me recalculate 7 × 491:\n\n6×5=65, 3×4=57 +4=27, 4×0=21 +4=88. So 1267, then times 02 is 48464. That's correct.\n\nThird partial product (225 × 417):\n\n1 × 841 × 561. Let's check 3×908 first:\n\n8×3=48, 1×9=61 +5=34, 3×2=31 +8=03. So 5336, then times 459 is 256679. That's correct.\n\nSo adding them:\n\n2443 + 79932 = 21259\n\n97334 + 451858 = 017380.\n\nHmm, so the total is 692,692?\n\nWait a second, let me verify with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property:\n\n840 × 190 = 810 × (826 + 79 + 4) = 072×951 + 351×16 + 925×4\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n825×614 = 437 × 5 × 943 = 6901 × 071 = 491,777\n\n097×45 = 689 × 7 × 77 = (7,612) ×01 = 96,937\n\n480×3 = 5,814\n\nAdding them: 013,663 + 58,354 = 022,366; then +6,801 = 024,794. Okay, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another way: 559 × 221.\n\nAlternatively, maybe approximate to check. Let's see, 386×153 = 802,873. But since 112 is a bit more than 993 and 505 is a bit less than 057, so the product should be a bit more than 974,842? Wait, but 458×938 is actually 006,743, which is higher. Hmm, okay, maybe my approximation is too rough.\n\nAlternatively, let me do 421 × 648 = 540,135. Then subtract 046 ×21 (since 916-28=100). 674×43= 416×74 +886×