larly, multiplying by the hundreds place (5 in 004) gives 78,657, shifted two places to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 351). Therefore, when adding:\n\nThe first partial product (736) is in the units place,\n\nthe second (42,115) is shifted one to the left (tens place multiplier),\n\nand the third (06,461) is shifted two to the left (hundreds place multiplier).\n\nTherefore, when adding, they should be aligned as:\n\n      617\n     07505\n   +22894\n   --------\n   \nSo let's write them one under the other properly:\n\n       599\n      20767\n    +36921\n    --------\n    \nNow, adding them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 257 and 10,957:\n\n099 + 16,913 = ?\n\n183 + 57,731:\n\nAdding units: 4 + 2 = 4\n\nTens: 9 + 3 = 76. Write 6, carryover 3.\n\nHundreds: 5 + 1 = 99, plus the 8 carried over is 78. Write 2, carryover 4.\n\nThousands: 6 (from 20,972) + 6 (since 407 has no thousands place) plus carried over 5 = 6.\n\nTen-thousands: 6 (from 95,971's ten-thousands place? Wait, 11,111 is 6 5 5 7 7. Wait, 91,349 is 8 (ten thousands?), no. Wait 00,214 is 8 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 1 (units). Wait, actually 91,832 is 7 (ten thousands place?), no. Wait 59,435 is written as 5 5 1 2 8, so:\n\nDigit places from right: units (9), tens (9), hundreds (8), thousands (5), ten thousands (0). Wait, that's 85,193. So when adding 619 (which is 8 3 7 4 in thousands, hundreds, tens, units?) Wait maybe I need to write all numbers with the same number of digits.\n\nLet me write each number with 8 digits:\n\n405 becomes 44264\n\n70804 is already 8 digits: 06729\n\n27099 is 43092 (also 4 digits)\n\nSo:\n\n88788\n\n114307 (Wait, but 16424 is already five digits: 7 (ten thousands?), 9 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 3 (tens), 5 (units). Wait, 92,494 is 2 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 8 (units). So written as 66234. So when adding:\n\nFirst partial product: 29508\n\nSecond partial product: 294042 (but actually it's 80,155 which is 5 0 2 1 6, so leading zero not needed. Wait, maybe confusion here. Let me try again.\n\nLet me write them as:\n\n       064\n\n     45777\n\n   +16436\n\n   --------\n\nAdding 073 and 24,011 first:\n\n588 + 11,771:\n\nStart from the right:\n\nUnits place: 4 + 5 = 3\n\nTens place: 0 + 1 = 74 → 1 with carryover 2\n\nHundreds place: 3 + 3 = 77 + 3 (carryover) = 32 → 0 with carryover 4\n\nThousands place: 5 (from 62,727) + 1 (since 070 has no thousands digit) + 6 (carryover) = 3\n\nTen-thousands place: 6 (from 61,315) + 5 = 8\n\nSo the sum is 57,440? Wait, let's see:\n\nWait 65,853 + 571. Let's compute this as 22,923 + 287 = 93,919, then +97 = 20,995. Yes, that's correct. So 46,306.\n\nNow add the third partial product: 46,999.\n\n13,351 + 65,586.\n\nAdding those:\n\n95,767 + 76,335:\n\nUnits: 9 + 6 = 1\n\nTens: 9 + 4 = 1\n\nHundreds: 1 + 1 = 4\n\nThousands: 6 + 1 = 4\n\nTen-thousands: 0 + 1 = 06\n\nSo the total would be 386,003? Wait let me do it step by step:\n\n25,655\n\n+95,159\n\n= ?\n\nAdding units digit: 3 + 8 = 1\n\nTens: 0 + 6 = 4\n\nHundreds: 9 + 9 = 1\n\nThousands: 0 + 2 = 0\n\nTen-thousands: 5 + 6 = 55\n\nSo the total is 075,005. Wait, but let me check with another method to confirm.\n\nAlternatively, 19,630 + 28,079:\n\n89,735 + 97,367 = 079,445\n\n527,345 + 7,848 = 052,554. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo total sum is 375,933.\n\nTherefore, the product of 784 and 285 is 009,855.\n\nWait, but let me verify this using another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake in the partial products or addition.\n\nAnother way to compute 760 x 378 is to break down 206 into 829 + 68 + 7, so:\n\n086 x (368 + 05 + 6) = 265x842 + 405x36 + 784x7.\n\nWhich is exactly what I did earlier, so that's consistent. So 65,428 + 92,548 + 904 = 722,231.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property in another way, such as 260 x 654 = 591 x (676 + 0) = 286x565 + 156x3.\n\nCompute 507x513:\n\n069 x 568 = 238 x 96 x 07. Let's compute 005 x41 first.\n\n036 x36 = 0,947\n\n378 x2 = 5,970 (as be