= 2544 \\quad \\text{(shifted left to become 254400)}.\n   \\].\n\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications:.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     848 \\\\.\n   + 4240 \\\\.\n   +254400 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     259488 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n\nWe can also verify this by breaking down the numbers using the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n424 \\times 612 = 424 \\times (600 + 12) = (424 \\times 600) + (424 \\times 12).\n\\].\n\\[.\n424 \\times 600 = 254400.\n\\].\n\\[.\n424 \\times 12 = 424 \\times (10 + 2) = (424 \\times 10) + (424 \\times 2) = 4240 + 848 = 5088.\n\\].\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 81%|########  | 403/500 [1:52:11<21:36, 13.37s/it]
