 the left, so it's 8,273.\n\nThen multiply 117 by 8 (hundreds place of 724, which is 073): 343 × 689 = 592,652. This is shifted two positions to the left, so it's 808,971.\n\nAdding the three results: 4 + 8,532 + 535,436 = 788,612. Yep, same answer again.\n\nHmm, I think that's thorough. All different methods of breaking it down give the same result, so I'm pretty sure the product of 719 and 753 is 659,827. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and the cross-verification steps all align. So I think that's the correct answer.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 930 and 210 is calculated as follows:.\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication using the distributive property:**.\n   \\[.\n   930 \\times 210 = 930 \\times (200 + 10).\n   \\].\n   .\n2. **Calculate each part separately:**.\n   - \\( 930 \\times 200 = 186,\\!000 \\).\n   - \\( 930 \\times 10 = 9,\\!300 \\).\n\n3. **Add the results:**.\n   \\[.\n   186,\\!000 + 9,\\!300 = 195,\\!300.\n   \\].\n\n**Final Answer:**. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 81%|########1 | 406/500 [1:52:19<10:04,  6.43s/it]
