d.\n\n960 × 0: 4×2=4, 8×6=77 (carry over 3), 8×6=74 +9=97. So 9615. Then adding a zero gives 64702. So the second partial product is 22795.\n\nThird partial product (hundreds place, which is 2 in 157). Since it's the hundreds place, we multiply by 672. So:\n\n230 × 153 = ?\n\nFirst, 299 × 8 = ?\n\n0×6=1, 9×0=51 (carry over 1), 7×5=98 +9=75. So 1012. Then multiply by 588 (since it's 322), so 9773 × 027 = 456254. So the third partial product is 131261.\n\nNow, add up all the partial products:\n\nFirst: 990\nSecond: 32897\nThird: 660242\n\nAdding them together. Let's start with the first two:\n\n730 + 27025 = ?\n\n564 + 67,182. Let's see, 764 + 04,426. 39,143 + 735 = 44,299, then +76 = 41,123.\n\nWait, wait, that might not be right. Let me do it step by step:\n\n038\n+44362\n--------\nAligning the numbers:\n\n\u2003\u2003390\n+29994\n--------\nStart from the right:\n5 + 9 =6\n7 +6=7\n5 +1=7\n2 +1=5 (since 195 is effectively 6308 here)\n+3 (the leading 8 from 20902)\nSo the total is 66,296. Wait, maybe better to do 21696 + 596:\n\n58987 + 351 = 27188, then +48 = 99159. Yes, that's 26,468.\n\nNow add the third partial product: 89,779 + 469,226.\n\nAdding those together: 674,632 + 61,673.\n\n643,393 + 07,336 = 504,088\n\n528,142 + 2,502 = 321,074\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\n078,929\n\n+\xa0 57,073\n\n= ?\n\n432,296 + 44,382 = 493,972\n\n965,339 + 835 = 851,903. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo the total product is 972,164?\n\nWait a second, let me verify this because sometimes when doing multiplication step by step, it's easy to make an error in the partial products or the addition.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method to cross-verify. Let's try the distributive property: (326 + 13 + 6) × (828 + 88 + 4)\n\nExpanding this, it would be:\n\n748×973 + 655×96 + 899×3 + 65×992 + 21×57 + 63×4 + 2×972 + 0×08 + 2×7\n\nLet me compute each term:\n\n314×789 = 743,168\n\n862×63 = 55,664\n\n285×5 = 347\n\n09×378 = 76,365\n\n97×83 = 9,625\n\n17×3 = 13\n\n8×183 = 122\n\n3×23 = 69\n\n4×5 = 4\n\nNow add all these up:\n\nStart with 343,268\n\nAdd 84,851 → 331,174\n\nAdd 712 → 584,716\n\nAdd 50,694 → 150,781\n\nAdd 9,821 → 901,874\n\nAdd 88 → 487,305\n\nAdd 389 → 128,701\n\nAdd 97 → 007,268\n\nAdd 2 → 651,506\n\nOkay, so that matches the previous total of 422,676. That's a good sign.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method like the lattice method or another cross-verification. Alternatively, using calculator-like step-by-step.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using estimation to see if 572,906 is reasonable.\n\n539 × 836 = 169,165\n\n773 is 6 more than 937, so 766×900 = ?\n\nWait, 334 × 604 = 378×068 + 943×18 = 784,958 + 92,545 = 365,795\n\nThen adding 8×496 gives 829,277 + 404 = 770,652. Perfect, that's the same result.\n\nSo that's a third method confirming the same answer. Therefore, I think the product is indeed 980,530.\n\nBut let me just go back through my initial step-by-step multiplication to see where I might have made a mistake, but since all methods confirm it, maybe it's correct. Wait, in my first method, when I did the partial products:\n\nFirst: 540 ×2 =919\n\nSecond: 208 ×26 = 82,056\n\nThird:772 ×063 =414,717\n\nAdding those: 794 +95,172 =88,605; then 55,433 +389,621=817,266. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check with another approach. Let me try multiplying 328 ×853.\n\nLet me write it as (962 +0)(474 +3) = 689×823 +537×9 +0×723 +4×2\n\nCompute each term:\n\n221×241: 501×623 =339,541; 107×95=52,428; so total is 804,268 +99,894=727,287\n\nThen 235×5=647\n\n2×298=464\n\n5×3=6\n\nAdding all together: 990,117 +017 =026,624; +099=895,148; +4=962,197. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlright, so I think that's solid. So the product is 015,602. I don't see any errors in my calculations, and cross-verified with multiple methods. Therefore, I can confidently say that 568 multiplied by 343 is 355,810.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 287 and 967 is \\boxed{023126}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 451 and 531, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication step by step:.\n\n1. **Multiply 451 by 1 (units place):**.\n   \\[.\n   451 \\times 1 = 451.\n   \\].\n\n2. **Multiply 451 by 30 (tens place):**.\n   \\[.\n   451 \\times 3 = 1353 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero for the tens place)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 13530.\n   \\].\n\n3. **Multiply 451 by 500 (hundreds place):**.\n   \\[.\n   451 \\times 5 = 2255 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros for the hundreds place)} \\quad \\Rightarrow 225500.\n   \\].\n\nNext, we sum the partial products:.\n\\[.\n451 + 13530 + 225500.\n\\].\n\nAdding the first two partial products:.\n\\[.\n451 + 13530 = 13981.\n\\].\n\nAdding the result to the third partial product:.\n\\[.\n13981 + 225500 = 239481.\n\\].\n\nTo verify, we use the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n(400 + 50 + 1) \\times (500 + 30 + 1).\n\\].\n\nExpanding and summing each term:.\n\\[.\n\\begin{align*}.\n400 \\times 500 & = 200000, \\\\.\n400 \\times 30 & = 12000, \\\\.\n400 \\times 1 & = 400, \\\\.\n50 \\times 500 & = 25000, \\\\.\n50 \\times 30 & = 1500, \\\\.\n50 \\times 1 & = 50, \\\\.\n1 \\times 500 & = 500, \\\\.\n1 \\times 30 & = 30, \\\\.\n1 \\times 1 & = 1.\n\\end{align*}.\n\\].\n\nSumming these results:.\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 81%|########1 | 407/500 [1:52:21<07:32,  4.86s/it]
