product of 848 and 331, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:.\n\n1. **Multiply 848 by the ones digit (1) of 331:**.\n   \\[.\n   848 \\times 1 = 848.\n   \\].\n   This gives the first partial product: 848.\n\n2. **Multiply 848 by the tens digit (3) of 331, shifted one position to the left:**.\n   \\[.\n   848 \\times 3 = 2544.\n   \\].\n   Shifting one position to the left gives the second partial product: 25440.\n\n3. **Multiply 848 by the hundreds digit (3) of 331, shifted two positions to the left:**.\n   \\[.\n   848 \\times 3 = 2544.\n   \\].\n   Shifting two positions to the left gives the third partial product: 254400.\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     848 \\\\.\n   +25440 \\\\.\n   +254400 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     280688 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n\n   - Adding 848 and 25440:.\n     \\[.\n     848 + 25440 = 26288.\n     \\].\n   - Adding the result to 254400:.\n     \\[.\n     26288 + 254400 = 280688.\n     \\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 84%|########3 | 418/500 [1:54:08<19:52, 14.55s/it]
