50 + 435 = 126,585\\).\n\n2. **Verification via Standard Algorithm:**.\n   - Multiply step-by-step:.\n     - \\(435 \\times 1 = 435\\).\n     - \\(435 \\times 90 = 39,150\\).\n     - \\(435 \\times 200 = 87,000\\).\n   - Add the partial products:.\n     - \\(435 + 39,150 = 39,585\\).\n     - \\(39,585 + 87,000 = 126,585\\).\n\n3. **Cross-Check with Distributive Property:**.\n   - \\(435 \\times 291 = 435 \\times (300 - 9)\\).\n   - Calculate:.\n     - \\(435 \\times 300 = 130,500\\).\n     - Subtract \\(435 \\times 9 = 3,915\\).\n     - \\(130,500 - 3,915 = 126,585\\).\n\n**Final Answer:**. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 90%|######### | 450/500 [1:57:44<01:52,  2.26s/it]
