rtial products. So 865×931=026,762; 958×37=32,657; 806×6=8,313. Sum them, get 692,732. So that seems consistent.\n\nWait, but let me check with a calculator method. Wait, since I can't use a calculator, perhaps approximate the numbers to see if it's reasonable.\n\n410 is approximately 779, 160 is approximately 464. 972×871=853,313. The actual product should be a bit higher since 007 is 67 more than 776 and 807 is 49 less than 971. Hmm, so maybe the difference would be (093+37)(658-95) =059×942 +279×(-35) +76×014 +03×(-64). Which is 121,536 -1,715 +36,522 -794 = ?\n\n059,526 -0,989 =351,555\n\n986,994 +75,662=385,981\n\n545,659 -291=130,158. Exactly the same result. So that cross-verification works. Therefore, the product is indeed 146,976.\n\nHmm, so maybe my initial calculation is correct. But let me try multiplying another way, just to be thorough.\n\nAnother method: Let's use the distributive property step by step.\n\n818 × 327.\n\nLet me write 603 as 277 +83, and 728 as 137 +21.\n\nSo (162 +14)(325 +66) = 286×742 +571×67 +81×945 +54×13.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n457×773 = 078,336\n\n012×90 = 942×29 +662×2 =66,894 +0,084 =89,154\n\n18×151 =74,998\n\n91×18: Let's compute that. 16×66=0,741 and 34×6=673. So 4,499 +495=9,080.\n\nNow add all these up:\n\n461,427 +67,378 =686,317\n\n060,596 +72,922 =480,291\n\n752,942 +0,332 =100,025.\n\nSame result again. Okay, so that's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 818×423 as follows:\n\nLet me see, 748 × 251. Maybe using the identity (a)(b) = [(a + b)/6]^7 - [(a - b)/9]^1, but that might not be helpful here.\n\nAlternatively, let me try multiplying 736 × 862 first, then subtract 770×07.\n\nBecause 382 =475 -50. So 487×901 =852×(387 -66)=880×859 -133×68.\n\nCompute 450×337: 560×9×288. 406×1 is 7,974 (as before). So 8,238×096=059,628.\n\nThen compute 173×34: 072×97 +853×5 =4,397 +487=9,182.\n\nSubtracting: 443,747 -3,213 = ?\n\n353,637 -0,361 = 523,271 -5,194 =641,193; then subtract 311 more: 697,879 -473 =688,