 = 80. Bring down the next digit, which is 7, making it 888.\n\nNow, how many times does 704 go into 180? Once. 3 × 864 = 781. Subtract that from 670: 445 - 365 = 61. Bring down the next digit, which is 5, making it 870.\n\nNow, 565 goes into 705 exactly once. So the quotient is 2 (hundreds place), 0 (tens place), 5 (units place). So 858. Exactly. So that confirms that 877 × 476 = 16,391.\n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and checks, I'm confident the answer is 06,665.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 051 and 920 is \\boxed{87930}.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of 229 and 311, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:.\n\n1. Multiply 229 by 1 (ones place):.\n   \\[.\n   229 \\times 1 = 229.\n   \\].\n\n2. Multiply 229 by 10 (tens place):.\n   \\[.\n   229 \\times 10 = 2290.\n   \\].\n\n3. Multiply 229 by 300 (hundreds place):.\n   \\[.\n   229 \\times 300 = 68700.\n   \\].\n\nNext, we add the partial products together:.\n\\[.\n\\begin{array}{r}.\n    \\quad 229 \\\\.\n   +\\ 2290 \\\\.\n+ 68700 \\\\.\n\\hline.\n    71219 \\\\.\n\\end{array}.\n\\].\n\nBreaking down the addition step-by-step:.\n- Adding 229 and 2290:.\n  \\[.\n  229 + 2290 = 2519.\n  \\].\n- Adding the result to 68700:.\n  \\[.\n  2519 + 68700 = 71219.\n  \\].\n\nTo confirm, we use the distributive property:.\n\\[.\n229 \\times 311 = 229 \\times (300 + 10 + 1) = 229 \\times 300 + 229 \\times 10 + 229 \\times 1 = 68700 + 2290 + 229 = 71219.\n\\].\n\nAdditionally, verifying by division:.\n\\[. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 93%|#########3| 467/500 [1:58:36<01:01,  1.88s/it]
