tive property:.\n- Break down 536 into 500 and 36:.\n  \\[.\n  794 \\times 536 = 794 \\times (500 + 36) = 794 \\times 500 + 794 \\times 36.\n  \\].\n- Calculate each part:.\n  \\[.\n  794 \\times 500 = 397000.\n  \\].\n  \\[.\n  794 \\times 36 = 23820 + 4764 = 28584.\n  \\].\n- Sum the results:.\n  \\[.\n  397000 + 28584 = 425584.\n  \\].\n\nBoth methods confirm the result. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 94%|#########4| 471/500 [1:59:15<04:40,  9.68s/it]
