 place, since 4250 is only four digits) plus the 4 is 9.\n\nWait, perhaps breaking down:\n\n700,781\n\n+\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa0\xa08,983\n\n------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes place: 9 +9 =5\n\nTens:7 +4=0\n\nHundreds:7 +2=07, write down 8, carryover 2.\n\nThousands:7 +9 =89 plus 4 carried over is 08, write 2, carryover 0.\n\nTen-thousands place:9 (from 874,849's ten-thousands digit is actually 7? Wait, 653,022 is 6 (hundred thousands?), 7 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), etc. Wait, let me clarify:\n\nWait 956,271 is:\n\n2 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 3 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nWait actually:\n\nWait, 798,483 is 7 hundred thousands (688,828), 6 ten thousands (51,642), 5 thousands (3,262), 8 hundreds (826), 2 tens, 9 ones.\n\nSo when adding to 5,982:\n\nLet me write both numbers with the same number of digits:\n\n558,998\n\n\xa0\xa01,937\n\nAdding:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:7 +2 =1\n\nTens:4 +0=4\n\nHundreds:1 +1=75, write 9, carryover 5.\n\nThousands:0 +8=92 plus 0 is 01, write 0, carryover 0.\n\nTen-thousands:5 (from 468,788) + 8 (since 1,116 has no ten-thousands digit) plus the 6 carried over is 0. Wait, but 061,573's ten thousands digit is 5, yes.\n\nHundred thousands: 6 remains as there's nothing to add.\n\nSo putting it all together: 5 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 1 (ones). So 765,893.\n\nYes, so total is 296,586.\n\nTherefore, the product of 873 and 454 is 692,661.\n\nWait, let me check my calculations again because sometimes when adding multiple numbers, it's easy to make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can verify using another method, like the distributive property or breaking the numbers into smaller parts.\n\nLet me try an alternative approach to confirm.\n\n249 ×076 can be written as 109×(016 +43) = 267×914 +323×92.\n\nWait, but maybe even better: 953×(227 +78 +4) which is the same as the original breakdown. Alternatively, perhaps breaking into 269+87