oduct of 039 and 815 is indeed 472,888.\n</think>.\n\nThe product of 850 and 130 is calculated as follows:.\n\n1. **Break down using the distributive property:**.\n   \\[.\n   850 \\times 130 = 850 \\times (100 + 30) = (850 \\times 100) + (850 \\times 30).\n   \\].\n   .\n2. **Calculate each part:**.\n   - \\(850 \\times 100 = 85,\\!000\\).\n   - \\(850 \\times 30 = 25,\\!500\\)  .\n     *(since \\(850 \\times 3 = 2,\\!550\\), then multiply by 10)*.\n\n3. **Sum the results:**.\n   \\[.\n   85,\\!000 + 25,\\!500 = 110,\\!500.\n   \\].\n\n**Final Answer:**. Therefore, my final answer is: "]] 99%|#########8| 493/500 [2:06:46<00:14,  2.14s/it]
