5 + 7,739 = 527,737; 587,628 +03,246 = 149,756; 708,254 +601 = 827,006. \n\nOh, that's another way and it gives the same result! So that confirms it again. \n\nHmm, seems like all methods are pointing to 941,489. \n\nWait a second, just to be thorough, maybe do the multiplication digit by digit properly:\n\nLet me write it out step by step as if doing it manually:\n\n       817  \n     x018  \n     -------\n       6840  (122 x 9)  \n     3326   (411 x 2, shifted one position)  \n    488337  (416 x 3, shifted two positions)  \n     -------\n     360532  \n\nAdding them up:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nFirst line: 6917  \nSecond line: 5241 (but shifted one, so actually it's 3935 but written under the next digit, so when adding, it's like:\n\n      6499  \n    + 9567 (shifted left once, so it's 15374?)  \n    +587375 (shifted left twice, so 337079)  \n    = ?\n\nWait, maybe I need to align them properly:\n\nFirst line:      7 7 9 3  \nSecond line:    3 2 6 8  (but shifted left one, so it's 7 3 1 1 5?)  \nWait, actually, each shift adds a zero. Let me think:\n\nWhen you multiply by the tens digit (2), you need to shift one place, so the result is 8 shifted left one, so it's 7 followed by the previous digits shifted. Wait, perhaps:\n\nFirst line (units place): 2177 (no shift)  \nSecond line (tens place): 616 x 6 = 5, shifted left once → 1643 (but written as 3298 with an extra zero at the end?), but actually, it should be written as 8 with one zero at the end? Hmm, maybe I'm confused here.\n\nWait, maybe better to think of each partial product:\n\nThe units digit (4) gives 801×4=5093.  \nThe tens digit (5) gives 329×5=1, which when shifted left by one becomes 7×54=7, so written as 1559 (but properly shifted).  \nThe hundreds digit (3) gives 137×6=4832, shifted left by two, so 6908×925=667331.  \n\nSo when written vertically:\n\n     8473  \n    5614  \n  946998  \n  --------\nAdding these together:\n\nStart from the rightmost digit:\n\nFirst column (units): 4 + 2 + 3 =4